EONC.push({
slug:"park-ji-yeon",img:"park-ji-yeon",short:"Park Ji-yeon",color:"#d98fa0",tags:["leader","eon"],epithet:"the Seoul team leader who married a quiet heir",
name:"Park Ji-yeon",fullName:"Park Ji-yeon (Mrs. Li Ji-yeon after her marriage)",
tagline:"A lonely Seoul team leader who fell for her sister’s quiet tutor, and found she had married the heir to a Shanghai empire.",
aliases:["Mrs. Li","Ji-yeon-ah","Unnie (to Soo-ah)","The Young Madam"],titles:["Madam of the Li Family","Former Marketing Team Leader","Closest Advisor to the Chairman of the Li Group"],
race:"Human",age:"Adult; in her late twenties at her wedding and in her fifties by the chronicle’s close, though she still looks about thirty",height:"Not specified; average height in the portrait",build:"Poised and brisk; the upright carriage of an office team leader",
hair:"Black and straight, usually in a high ponytail with loose strands framing her face",eyes:"Dark and sharp, with a confident winged line",
origin:"Seoul, South Korea",affiliation:"The Li family of Shanghai and its conglomerate, the Li Group; formerly a Seoul cosmetics company; the Dreamer’s Catalogue",role:"Wife of the Li heir; former marketing team leader; later the Chairman’s closest advisor",
sagas:["seoul"],firstSaga:"seoul",status:"Alive; at the Chairman’s side in Seoul",
caption:"Park Ji-yeon in a grey sleeveless turtleneck and dark trousers, hands at her hips and hair in a high ponytail, smiling in a bright Seoul office.",
tier:"t7",stats:{off:3,def:3,spd:4,mys:3,utl:10,rea:4},
note:"**A world without magic.** Ji-yeon comes from a world with no qi, gods or spells. Her chronicle is a modern family saga, so her ‘powers’ are those of an extraordinary mortal: a boardroom mind, an iron will and a devotion that behaves almost like a law of nature, plus one quietly uncanny gift, a beauty that refuses to age. She sits in the **Luminary** tier of the ranking, the tier for people of worlds without magic.",
intro:"**Park Ji-yeon** is a Seoul marketing team leader in her late twenties: capable, respected, overworked and quietly lonely, until the soft-spoken university student who tutors her younger sister becomes the safest place in her life. She falls for him believing they will have to count every won together. Only later does she learn that Eon is the hidden heir of the Li family of Shanghai. Married on a golden October day, she leaves her career to stand beside him, raises three children and becomes the most formidable presence in every boardroom her husband enters. She simply cannot be separated from him, and she does not appear to age.",
bio:[
{h:"A lonely team leader",t:"Ji-yeon grew up in an ordinary Seoul family with her parents and her younger sister, Soo-ah. By her late twenties she was a team leader in the marketing department of a cosmetics company: sharp, dependable and always the last to leave. Her evenings were late trains, a careful ramyeon budget and an empty apartment. Her colleagues knew her as a stressed, exacting leader; she privately wondered whether anyone would ever truly see her."},
{h:"The quiet tutor",t:"Eon came into her life through the front door of her family’s modest apartment, as the tutor hired to help Soo-ah with her studies. He was a Chinese university student living in Seoul: tall, calm, simply dressed and kind in a way that asked for nothing. He never spoke about his family.\n\nJi-yeon noticed him first as the only person who noticed when she was exhausted. When overwork finally caught up with her and she collapsed, he was the one who stayed with her. She fell in love with the quiet, hardworking student, and made plans to save, with him, for a small apartment of their own."},
{h:"The heir revealed",t:"The truth came out gradually: the Gangnam penthouse, a sports car he almost never drove, a family jet, and a family in Shanghai whose business spanned trade, real estate and technology. Eon was the only son and heir of the Li family. Ji-yeon was, by her own account, ‘so angry at first’; she had been ready to struggle beside him. Then she understood why he had hidden it: he wanted to be loved for himself. As Eon later put it in his vows, ‘you chose me when you thought I had nothing’.\n\nIn Shanghai, Mr. and Mrs. Li welcomed her as a daughter, set the wedding for the 18th of October and gave the couple a newly built mansion on the family’s hillside estate. Touring its long hallways, Ji-yeon grew anxious that a house so large might put distance between them. Eon told her that she was his home, not the walls around them, and she relaxed at once."},
{h:"Telling the Parks",t:"Back in Seoul, Ji-yeon invited her parents and Soo-ah to dinner without saying where. The private elevator opened onto the penthouse’s grand piano and night view of the city, and her family froze. She told them everything, from the student she had first loved to the heir she was about to marry.\n\nSoo-ah shrieked that her sister had ‘hit the jackpot’. Her mother had to sit down. Her father said quietly that money did not matter as long as Eon treated her well, but that he was glad she would not have to struggle. Later her mother pulled her aside in the kitchen: even if he had nothing, she said, she could see from the way he looked at her daughter that he truly loved her."},
{h:"The eighteenth of October",t:"The wedding joined two countries in one day. In the morning, at an outdoor venue by the Han River dressed in white flowers and autumn leaves, Ji-yeon walked down the aisle on her father’s arm before some three hundred guests. Her vows thanked Eon for seeing her when she was stressed and lonely and for staying when she collapsed, and promised to protect him fiercely. At the reception her former colleagues barely recognised the radiant woman their old team leader had become.\n\nThat evening the family flew to Shanghai for a grand banquet at the Li estate. In a red Chinese wedding qipao, Ji-yeon served tea to Eon’s parents and called them ‘Mom’ and ‘Dad’ through happy tears; Mrs. Li embraced her and said, ‘You are our daughter now.’ The night closed with a second first dance under the garden lanterns."},
{h:"The Bund incident",t:"A few days later, at a skyscraper restaurant above the Bund, Ji-yeon refused the seat across the table and sat beside her husband instead. Midway through dinner she calmly told him she was going to resign and follow him everywhere, to lectures, family business and every duty of the young master. If he said no, she added with a sweet smile, she would throw a tantrum, and she was not joking in the slightest.\n\nMinutes later a nervous waiter served Eon the one dish he had asked to avoid, and a splash of hot sauce left a tiny red mark on his finger. Ji-yeon rose in icy fury. The manager bowed, apologised, waived the bill and brought out the head chef to cook a new dish personally. ‘I’m sorry for causing a scene,’ she told Eon afterwards, ‘but I won’t apologise for protecting you.’ The morning after they returned to Seoul, she resigned by video call and politely declined a promotion meant to keep her."},
{h:"A family of five",t:"Two weeks after her resignation, Ji-yeon learned she was expecting, and spent the entire day refusing to let go of her husband. Their daughter was born in a private maternity suite in Seoul with Eon at her side throughout, her hand never leaving his. She named the baby **Li Eun-seo**: ‘Eun for grace and kindness, like her father. Seo for gentle and beautiful.’\n\nA son, **Li Jun-ho**, followed four years later, and a second daughter, **Li Ye-na**, about eight years into the marriage. Ji-yeon raised them in the Gangnam penthouse to be humble despite their wealth: Eun-seo grew into a gracious young woman who thanked staff by name and spoke Korean and Mandarin with equal ease. At every family gathering, a running joke repeated itself: Mrs. Li would playfully reach for a snack near Eon, and Ji-yeon would wrap both arms around her husband. ‘Mother, you can have anything on the table… but not my husband.’"},
{h:"Madam of the Li Group",t:"Twenty-one years after the wedding, Eon’s father named him head of the family empire, and soon handed him complete control of a conglomerate spanning trade, real estate, renewable energy and technology. Ji-yeon went with him everywhere: board meetings, overseas trips, formal dinners. She sat beside him in a navy dress, passed him water, offered marketing and branding insight, and steered every discussion toward the best terms for him.\n\nHer patience had limits. At one Shanghai board meeting, after two and a half hours, she rose and informed the executives, with a polite and glacial smile, that her husband had given them more than enough time and the rest could be handled by email. During a twelve-billion-dollar joint venture with a European conglomerate, she pushed back against a 60–40 split, demanded at least 70–30, and kept pushing every time Eon tried to calm her. The deal closed at 72–28 with strong technology protections, and the European team left looking dazed. Eun-seo heard the story from her father’s secretary and laughed until she cried."},
{h:"The nest that was not empty",t:"When Ye-na was accepted into Seoul National University’s arts programme, Ji-yeon completed what the family called her ‘independence spree’: in a single month she bought each of her children a furnished apartment, a car, a trust fund and a security team. She cried a little in the car after Ye-na moved out. Then she walked back into the penthouse and declared it, happily, ‘my place with you’ again.\n\nShe remained a devoted mother. The family still gathered two or three times a month for her Korean-Chinese feasts, where the children teased their parents about their legendary affection. ‘Mama is the most in-love person I know,’ Ye-na said."},
{h:"Later years",t:"In time, both sets of grandparents passed away, one by one. Through every farewell, Ji-yeon was Eon’s anchor, and he was hers: ‘As long as I have you, I can endure anything.’ Eon became sole chairman of the Li Group. When he asked his children about succession, none of them wanted the whole empire: Eun-seo preferred strategy and branding, Jun-ho operations, and Ye-na her illustrations. Ji-yeon settled the matter warmly: their father had built the empire, and he would decide when and how to pass it on.\n\nThe chronicle closes with Jun-ho’s wedding to Choi Soo-min only two weeks away, and Ji-yeon, still looking no older than thirty-three, at her husband’s side for the final suit fitting, as she has been at his side for everything else."}],
appearance:"Ji-yeon has straight black hair, most often pulled up into a high ponytail with loose strands falling around her face, and sharp, expressive dark eyes finished with a confident winged line. A small beauty mark sits just below the corner of her lips. Her expression rests in a warm, faintly knowing half-smile, the look of someone who has already decided how the meeting will end.\n\nIn the portrait she stands in a bright modern office, shelves and equipment soft-focused behind her, wearing a grey ribbed sleeveless turtleneck and dark trousers, hands resting at her hips. For her wedding she wore a white gown with a long train and an elegant updo; at the Shanghai banquet, a red Chinese wedding qipao; in later years, cheongsam-style dresses at the Li estate and a navy dress in the boardroom.\n\nHer most remarked-upon feature is time itself: at forty-seven she looked barely thirty, and at fifty-two no older than thirty-three.",
personality:[
{h:"Devoted beyond measure",t:"Eon is the organising principle of Ji-yeon’s life. ‘Let me be your shadow,’ she tells him, and she means it: she gave up a career to stand beside him and dislikes even short separations. If he is out of her sight for more than half a minute at a party, she goes looking for him, and she finds him."},
{h:"Sweet on the surface, steel underneath",t:"She speaks softly, smiles often and almost never raises her voice. But when her mind is made up there is, as the story puts it, steel beneath the sweetness. Her calmest smiles are usually the ones that precede an ultimatum."},
{h:"Fiercely protective",t:"A tiny burn on her husband’s finger is, to Ji-yeon, a crisis. She is the first to stand between him and any inconvenience, and the last to accept an apology. She does not apologise for it either."},
{h:"Selfless, for him",t:"She has no interest in personal gain. Every advantage in every deal should go to Eon; what is good for him, she reasons, is good for her and their children. Her ambition is entirely aimed at someone else."},
{h:"A warm mother and daughter",t:"She cooks lavish Korean-Chinese feasts, fusses over her children long after they are grown, helps Mrs. Li in the kitchen and taught all three children humility despite their wealth. Her one rule for her daughters is that they should wait for someone worth fighting for."},
{h:"Fears",t:"Her deepest fear is going back to the empty apartment and endless late nights of her twenties: being alone, unseen and tired. Her second is anything, however small, happening to Eon."}],
powersIntro:"Ji-yeon has no qi, spells or divine light. What she has is a relentless mind, a voice that ends meetings, a fortune she wields with precision and a devotion that operates with the reliability of a law of nature. One gift is genuinely uncanny: across three decades of her chronicle she barely ages. Every name below was coined for this wiki except where marked.",
powers:[
{cat:"Devotion & Protection",blurb:"The heart of everything she does.",items:[
P("The Shadow Vow","e","Core","A total, lifelong commitment to remain at Eon’s side: every lecture, meeting, journey and dinner, for decades.","Sworn aloud at the Bund restaurant (‘Let me be your shadow’) and kept from that day on; she reorganises her entire life around his schedule without friction.","She cannot bear long separations; when he must go somewhere alone, she asks whether she may at least wait in the car.","Resigns from her career the morning after returning to Seoul, then accompanies him to every board meeting and overseas trip for more than twenty years."),
P("Guardian’s Fury","e","Peak","An instant, overwhelming protective response to anything that harms or inconveniences Eon, from a careless waiter to an unfair contract.","Her calm switches to ice in a heartbeat; she speaks low, precise and immovable, and keeps going until the problem is fixed.","Eon is the only one who can soften it, with a hand on her arm, though she may simply resume afterwards.","Turns a tiny hot-sauce splash at a luxury Bund restaurant into a full apology from the manager, a waived bill and the head chef cooking a new dish personally.","The tantrum"),
P("Not Up for Borrowing","s","Support","A lightning-fast reflex that pulls Eon into her arms whenever anyone, even family, reaches toward him in jest.","Pure instinct; it fires before she has time to think, then dissolves into a sweet but serious smile.","Harmless and good-humoured; it only ever blocks hugs, snacks and teasing.","Becomes a decades-long family joke: ‘Anything except my husband. He is not up for borrowing.’"),
P("Homing Heart","e","Support","An uncanny ability to find Eon in any crowd, house or venue.","After about thirty seconds without seeing him, she follows an unerring instinct straight to him.","Comes at the cost of real anxiety until she finds him.","Crosses a packed graduation party to his exact location within moments.")]},
{cat:"Boardroom Arts",blurb:"A team leader’s mind, sharpened by an empire.",items:[
P("Steel Beneath Silk","e","Peak","Negotiation of frightening effectiveness: she reads the table, names the fair price and refuses to move until the other side does.","She opens with warm courtesy, lays out the long-term value her side brings, then holds her figure through every counter-offer.","Can come across as too aggressive; Eon sometimes has to pause her, and she resumes ten minutes later.","Turns a European conglomerate’s proposed 60–40 split on a twelve-billion-dollar joint venture into a 72–28 deal with technology protections."),
P("The Meeting Is Over","e","Core","The authority to end any meeting on her husband’s behalf, and have the room accept it.","A polite, glacial smile and a single sentence: the remaining details can be handled by email.","Used only when a meeting has run long past its value; she always takes Eon with her.","Closes a tense Shanghai board meeting after two and a half hours; the executives later reconvene better prepared."),
P("Advantage Sense","e","Support","Spots, almost instantly, when someone is trying to take a little more than their share.","Years of marketing negotiations have given her an ear for imbalance in terms, prices and vendors.","Applies to the Li family’s interests; she does not care about her own.","Catches a wedding planner proposing a costlier but worse vendor for Jun-ho’s wedding."),
P("Campaign Mind","e","Support","Marketing and branding expertise that shapes strategy across the Li Group.","Drawn from her years as a cosmetics-company team leader; offered quietly at Eon’s side.","Advisory; she never seeks a title of her own.","Advises Eon from his first remote meetings with Shanghai onwards; her eldest daughter later rises in the family’s international marketing division."),
P("The Independence Spree","s","Peak","Deploys great wealth with speed and precision to transform lives in a single stroke.","She researches, chooses, furnishes and secures everything herself.","Only as good as the planning behind it, and she plans everything.","In one month gives each of her three children a furnished apartment, a car, a trust fund and a security team.")]},
{cat:"Hearth & Family",blurb:"The quieter powers of the Li household.",items:[
P("Hearth of Gangnam","e","Core","Turns any residence into a warm, well-run home.","Cooking, decorating and organising; she learns new recipes constantly.","Needs her family around her to work at full strength.","Hosts Korean-Chinese feasts that draw three grown children home two or three times a month."),
P("Seamless Grace","e","Support","Handles a husband, three children and a full social calendar at once without a visible seam.","Practised timing and flawless precision; she always knows where everyone is.","Exhausting for anyone else to imitate.","Gets three children ready for a park day while never leaving Eon’s side."),
P("Mother’s Compass","e","Support","Raises children who stay humble and kind despite immense wealth.","Example rather than lecture: warmth, gratitude and love on display every day.","Cannot make anyone want the family empire; none of her children choose to lead it.","Eun-seo grows into a gracious young woman who thanks staff by name and helps set the table at her grandparents’ mansion.")]},
{cat:"The Unfading",blurb:"The one gift no one can explain.",items:[
P("Unfading Spring","e","Peak","She does not visibly age: decades pass and she only grows more elegant.","Unexplained in the story; the family attributes it to happiness.","No known limit; it affects appearance and energy, not lifespan or strength.","Looks barely thirty at forty-seven, and no older than thirty-three at fifty-two."),
P("Room-Stilling Presence","e","Support","An aura of composed elegance that quiets a room when she enters.","Poise, confidence and complete certainty of where she belongs.","Strongest in formal settings: banquets, galas and boardrooms.","Turns heads even among the wealthy relatives of the Li family in Shanghai."),
P("Anchor Heart","e","Core","Emotional resilience that carries her and her family through pain and grief.","Her bond with Eon is the anchor: ‘As long as I have you, I can endure anything.’","Depends entirely on him being there.","Endures a long labour holding his hand, and steadies the family through the loss of all four grandparents.")]}],
relationships:[
{who:"eon",name:"Eon",kind:"Husband",text:"The quiet university student who tutored her sister and turned out to be the heir of the Li family of Shanghai. She married him on the 18th of October and has not left his side since."},
{who:"li-eun-seo",name:"Li Eun-seo",kind:"Eldest daughter",text:"Elegant, humble and bilingual; later an executive in the family’s international division. ‘I want what Mom and Dad have.’"},
{who:"li-jun-ho",name:"Li Jun-ho",kind:"Son",text:"An athletic, good-natured swimmer who goes on to run operations for the family business, and is engaged to Choi Soo-min."},
{who:"li-ye-na",name:"Li Ye-na",kind:"Youngest daughter",text:"The bubbly artist of the family, who studies fine arts at Seoul National University and becomes an illustrator."},
{who:"park-soo-ah",name:"Park Soo-ah",kind:"Younger sister",text:"The student Eon was hired to tutor, and the first to tease the couple. Her verdict on learning the truth: ‘Unnie, you hit the jackpot!’"},
{who:"mrs-li",name:"Mrs. Li",kind:"Mother-in-law",text:"Eon’s warm mother, who called Ji-yeon ‘our daughter’ at the wedding and has been jokingly reaching for snacks near Eon ever since."},
{who:"parks",name:"Mr. and Mrs. Park",kind:"Parents",text:"Her parents, who only wanted her to be happy, and were very glad she would not have to struggle."},
{who:"su-eon-lingwei",kind:"Fellow member of the Catalogue",text:"[[su-eon-lingwei|Lingwei]] and Ji-yeon both help steer a conglomerate beside Eon, one with frost and one with a boardroom smile."}],
trivia:["Her wedding joined two ceremonies in one day: a Korean ceremony by the Han River with about 300 guests, and a Chinese banquet at the Li estate in Shanghai.","Before she learned the truth about Eon, she was budgeting for ramyeon and saving for a small apartment for the two of them.","Her daughter’s name means ‘grace and kindness’ (Eun) and ‘gentle and beautiful’ (Seo).","She always sits beside her husband, never across from him, even at a table set for two.","Her children agree that ‘Mom is scarier than any villain when it comes to Dad.’","She was the first character on this wiki from a world without magic or cultivation, and the first in the Luminary tier."],
quotes:[["I would have loved him even if he had nothing.","Telling her family the truth about Eon"],["I’m sorry for causing a scene. But I won’t apologise for protecting you.","After the Bund restaurant incident"],["Mother, you can have anything on the table… but not my husband.","At tea with Mrs. Li"],["You are my world, Eon. Everything else… is just scenery.","In later years"],["Ji-yeon, you chose me when you thought I had nothing.","Eon’s wedding vow"]]
});
EONC.push({
slug:"hamazaki-risa",img:"hamazaki-risa",short:"Hamazaki Risa",color:"#e3a15f",tags:["eon"],epithet:"the campus gal who befriended a lone otaku",
name:"Hamazaki Risa",fullName:"Hamazaki Risa (Risa Hamazaki in Western name order)",
tagline:"The most popular gal on campus spotted one anime clip on a quiet student’s phone, and decided he was worth knowing.",
aliases:["Risa","Hamazaki-san","The Sun of the Literature Department"],titles:["Campus Gal of the Literature Department","Eon’s Closest Friend","Karaoke Champion (self-declared)"],
race:"Human",age:"Adult; a university student in the same literature department as Eon (exact age not given)",height:"Not specified; noted as tall for a Japanese woman, taller still in platform sneakers",build:"Slender and confident, with a bouncy, unhurried gal stride",
hair:"Dyed light brown, falling in loose, stylish waves past her shoulders; sometimes a loose ponytail tied with a ribbon",eyes:"Sharp and expressive, finished with bold winged eyeliner; noticeably softer when she looks at Eon",
origin:"Tokyo, Japan (lives in a university dormitory)",affiliation:"Literature department of a Tokyo university",role:"University student; the most popular gal on campus; Eon’s closest friend",
sagas:["nakano"],firstSaga:"nakano",status:"Alive; Eon’s closest friend, quietly hoping for more",
caption:"Hamazaki Risa on a sunny campus walkway, winking and waving as she reaches out a hand, in a white camisole and denim shorts, long light-brown hair loose.",
tier:"t7",stats:{off:2,def:3,spd:5,mys:1,utl:8,rea:3},
note:"**A world without magic.** Risa’s chronicle is a modern campus story with no spells, gods or systems. Like [[park-ji-yeon|Park Ji-yeon]] she sits in the **Luminary** tier, and her ‘powers’ are the talents of an extraordinary young woman: a gal’s charisma, fearless social initiative, a secretly encyclopaedic love of anime and a heart far softer than her tongue.",
intro:"**Hamazaki Risa** is the brightest star of a Tokyo university’s literature department: tall, fashionable, blunt and permanently surrounded by friends. Nobody suspects that she quietly tracks and rates every anime season. One Thursday afternoon she glances at the phone of the quiet student a few seats away, recognises the show he is watching, and leans over to ask about it. That student is Eon, a gamer who loves nothing more than a quiet evening alone. Within a month she has dragged him to Akihabara, a late-night screening and an anime convention; within a year she is his closest friend, and secretly a little in love with him.",
bio:[
{h:"The sun of the literature department",t:"Risa is the kind of student a campus arranges itself around. She is tall and stylish, with light-brown waves, sharp eyeliner and platform sneakers, and wherever she sits a small group gathers to laugh at her jokes, ask for skincare advice or beg her to come to weekend karaoke. Half the young men in the literature department, the story notes, orbit her like planets.\n\nBeneath the bright surface she is sharper than people expect: direct, funny and allergic to fake politeness. She also keeps a secret she has never bothered to explain to her friends. She loves anime, rates every series in a tracking app, and is tired of people assuming that someone who looks like her only cares about makeup and dating."},
{h:"“…Is that Shield Hero?”",t:"One Thursday afternoon, in a lecture called *Modern Media and Narrative Analysis*, Risa arrives late, finds her usual friends absent and takes a seat closer than usual to a quiet student in a hoodie by the window. He is watching the newest episode of an isekai series on his phone, hidden behind his notebook. She recognises it instantly.\n\n‘…Is that Shield Hero?’ she asks, just loud enough for him to hear.\n\nThe student is Eon, who has never in his life expected the most popular woman in the department to speak to him, let alone about his favourite show. For the rest of the lecture they trade whispered opinions whenever the professor turns to the board: the new party member is annoying, the light novel handled the arc better, the animation budget has finally arrived."},
{h:"“Don’t ghost me, otaku-kun”",t:"When class ends, Risa does not leave. She asks him to explain a season finale a friend once spoiled for her, and they talk for forty minutes on a bench beside the campus garden, cherry petals still on the ground. She shows him her ratings (one isekai at 9.2, Shield Hero at 8.4, a comedy she has just finished) and challenges him to fight her over the order. She admits that she likes stories where the underdog flips the script, because in real life people look down on her for how she looks and talks.\n\nThen she holds out her phone for his messaging ID. ‘Don’t ghost me, otaku-kun. I know where your class is.’ That night it is Risa who sends the first message. Soon come screenshots, reactions typed in capital letters, and a dramatic voice note re-enacting the worst isekai cliché she can think of."},
{h:"A month of bold invitations",t:"Risa does not wait to be invited anywhere. On a rainy afternoon she catches Eon before he can escape to the station and takes him to a new anime-goods pop-up in Akihabara, where he explains the difference between figure materials and she makes him try on a cat-ear headband, laughs until people turn to look, and buys it for him as a joke gift. Over crepes she asks whether he really lives completely alone.\n\nShe buys two tickets to a late-night anime film screening in Shinjuku before asking whether he is free, quietly cries during the emotional scenes, and punches his shoulder afterwards: ‘Don’t tell anyone I cried, got it?’ Over ramen, she admits she expected him to run away when she first spoke to him, and finds it refreshing that he never tries to act cool. Karaoke for two, library study sessions and coffee-shop ranking debates follow."},
{h:"Odaiba",t:"Her boldest request is a Sunday at a huge two-day anime convention in Odaiba. Conventions are Eon’s sacred territory, and bringing her feels like showing someone a secret room. Risa meets him at ten, approves of his outfit (‘Progress’), lets him lead her through the indie artists’ alleys and leads him through the merchandise halls in return. She buys a plush for herself and a matching keychain for him ‘so we match’, and links arms with him when the crowd gets thick.\n\nIn a raffle queue she asks him, seriously, whether her dragging him out bothers him, because she knows how much he loves his time alone. He admits it did at first, and that now he does not hate it at all. ‘Good,’ she says. ‘Because I like hanging out with you. You’re real.’"},
{h:"The kingdom’s first guest",t:"Months pass. Summer heat gives way to autumn, and Risa and Eon become the kind of friends who text every day and meet three or four times a week. When he says he needs a night to recharge, she answers ‘Got it. Don’t stay up too late gaming,’ and simply carries on the next day.\n\nOne October evening she finally visits his tiny apartment in Nakano, the place he calls his kingdom. She admires his figure collection, helps him rearrange the shelves for better lighting, eats sushi on the floor and watches a new series with him. Somewhere in the middle of the second episode she realises she is watching him more than the screen. The confident gal, to her own annoyance, has become shy."},
{h:"Lights by the tower",t:"The feelings do not go away. At a November convention she insists on matching keychains for their bags. In early December they walk beneath the Christmas illuminations near Tokyo Tower; she wants very much to take his hand and instead tells him to stop staring at the lights before he trips. When he asks if she is all right, she claims she is cold and tells him to walk faster.\n\nTheir friends notice before Eon does. One of his club friends cannot believe Eon is close to someone so ‘campus level’. Another, Yumi, quietly tells Risa that she looks at him differently now. Risa denies it on the spot, then lies awake in her dormitory and admits to herself that she is falling for him."},
{h:"Snow and a half-confession",t:"On a cold January night, over a winter hotpot and a cosy anime marathon under one shared blanket, Risa stops calling him ‘otaku-kun’. Using his name for once, she tells him that these months have been nicer than she ever expected, that he is different from other people because he never pretends, and that around him she sometimes feels shy, which is ridiculous because she is never shy. ‘I like spending time with you,’ she says. ‘A lot.’\n\nEon, honest and still a little oblivious, tells her he likes spending time with her too, and that it means a great deal that she respects his time alone. It is not a confession, and it is not a rejection. Risa leans her shoulder against his and decides that, for now, being his closest friend is enough. Outside, snow begins to fall over Tokyo."}],
appearance:"Risa is tall for a Japanese woman and carries it with a confident, slightly bouncy stride. Her dyed light-brown hair falls in loose waves past her shoulders, and her makeup is always precise: sharp winged eyeliner, glossy lips and a touch of highlighter on the cheekbones. Her eyes are sharp and quick, though people who know her notice they soften whenever she talks to Eon. Her voice is a little husky.\n\nIn the portrait she stands on a sunlit campus walkway, giving the viewer a playful wink and a small, knowing smile as she waves with one hand and reaches out with the other. Her long brown hair is loose, and she wears a white camisole, denim shorts and silver drop earrings.\n\nHer wardrobe is unmistakably gal: a cropped white hoodie, a pleated skirt and platform sneakers on the day she first speaks to Eon; an oversized jacket, high-waisted shorts, comfortable trainers and a ribboned ponytail for the convention; a stylish winter coat for the December lights. She carries a designer-style bag and, after the first convention, a keychain that matches one on Eon’s backpack.",
personality:[
{h:"Bold, blunt and teasing",t:"Risa says exactly what she thinks. She can switch from bubbly laughter to deadpan sarcasm in a heartbeat, roasts bad recommendations without mercy and answers disagreement with a cheerful ‘Fight me.’ She has no patience for flattery or pretence, and very little for people who try too hard to impress her."},
{h:"Considerate underneath",t:"Her teasing hides real thoughtfulness. She asks genuine, pointed questions and listens to the answers. She noticed early that Eon needs time alone to recharge, and she protects it, even when she would rather see him. She is also the one who stops to ask whether she is intruding."},
{h:"A secret otaku",t:"She loves anime with complete sincerity and keeps that side of herself low-key on campus, tired of being judged by her looks. With Eon she can finally argue about adaptations, rank seasons and rewatch favourite scenes without explaining herself."},
{h:"Shy only with him",t:"The one person who can make the most confident gal on campus go quiet is a soft-spoken gamer. Around Eon she blushes when their hands brush, loses her words during romantic scenes and hides behind excuses about the cold. She dislikes this about herself and would never admit it to anyone else."},
{h:"Fears",t:"She fears being seen only as a pretty face, and, more recently, saying too much too soon and losing the friendship that has become the best part of her week."}],
powersIntro:"Risa has no magic, no system and no secret lineage. What she has is the presence of a campus star, the nerve to make every first move, a hidden otaku’s encyclopaedic memory and the rarer skill of knowing when to step back. Every name below was coined for this wiki except where marked.",
powers:[
{cat:"Gal Charisma",blurb:"The presence that makes a campus turn its head.",items:[
P("Campus Sunshine","e","Core","A natural magnetism that draws people into her orbit wherever she goes.","Confidence, style and quick humour; she never seems to be trying, which is the point.","It attracts attention she does not always want, from pushy seniors to people who think they already know her.","A small crowd follows her between lectures; half the young men in the department are said to revolve around her."),
P("Sunshine-to-Deadpan Switch","e","Core","An instant change of tone, from bright laughter to bone-dry sarcasm, that wins arguments and ends unwanted conversations.","Pure timing; she reads the moment and flips the mood before the other person has caught up.","Can sting people who do not know her well.","Turns away an insistent senior by announcing that she only talks to people who can name three isekai with decent world-building. ‘He looked like I spoke alien.’"),
P("Gal Polish","e","Support","Fashion and makeup skill that makes every outfit look effortless.","Years of practice: sharp eyeliner, confident colour choices and outfits planned for the day’s adventure.","Takes time; a rainy day can still ruin her hair.","Turns up to a full day at an anime convention perfectly dressed for walking, and still looks striking.")]},
{cat:"Social Initiative",blurb:"Risa makes the first move, every time.",items:[
P("The First Move","e","Peak","A fearless willingness to start any conversation, friendship or plan herself.","She simply asks, directly and without hesitation, and lets the other person catch up.","Relies on reading people well; she can overwhelm someone who is very shy.","Speaks to Eon mid-lecture, keeps him talking for forty minutes, asks for his messaging ID and sends the first message that same night."),
P("Two Tickets Already","e","Peak","Invitations that arrive as accomplished facts, so that saying no would mean wasting a ticket.","She books first and asks second, always with a teasing ‘Don’t say no.’","She is careful to use it on fun, never on anything he would truly dislike.","Buys two tickets to a late-night film screening in Shinjuku before asking whether Eon is free."),
P("Don’t Ghost Me","s","Support","A steady stream of messages, screenshots and voice notes that keeps a new friendship warm.","Daily check-ins at random hours, always with something to react to.","Only works on someone who answers back, which Eon does.","‘Don’t ghost me, otaku-kun. I know where your class is.’ Within weeks, she is sending voice notes almost every evening."),
P("Cave-Day Radar","e","Core","An instinct for when someone needs to be left alone, and the discipline to respect it.","She notices the signals, steps back gracefully and returns the next day as if nothing happened.","It costs her something; she would usually rather stay.","Answers Eon’s ‘I need to recharge tonight’ with ‘Got it. Don’t stay up too late gaming,’ and never once makes him feel guilty for it.")]},
{cat:"Secret Otaku Arts",blurb:"The side of Risa only Eon really sees.",items:[
P("The Secret Tracker","e","Core","A detailed, honest memory of every series she has watched, rated and argued about.","A tracking app, strong opinions and a willingness to defend them.","She keeps it hidden from most of her friends.","Defends her ranking of one isekai at 9.2 and Shield Hero at 8.4 against Eon, and debates the differences between light-novel and web-novel versions of a story."),
P("Whisper Commentary","e","Support","Running commentary so sharp and well timed that the person beside her has to fight not to laugh.","A low voice, a straight face and perfect timing during lectures and screenings.","Risky in front of strict professors.","Makes Eon stifle laughter through a whole week of media lectures."),
P("Roast, Then Binge","e","Support","Merciless criticism of a recommendation, followed by watching all of it anyway.","Honesty first, curiosity second.","Her reviews can be brutal.","Tears apart a lesser-known series Eon recommends, then admits she binge-watched every episode.")]},
{cat:"Play & Performance",blurb:"Where the gal and the otaku meet.",items:[
P("Karaoke Queen","e","Peak","A genuinely skilled singing voice for pop and anime songs.","Practice, confidence and a love of the stage.","Unfortunately for Eon, she expects duets.","Sings energetic songs with surprising skill, then applauds Eon’s shy, off-key attempt: ‘You’re terrible but it’s cute.’"),
P("Crowd Navigator","e","Support","Moves through packed streets and convention halls with complete ease, and brings her friends with her.","She picks a direction, links arms when the crowd is dense, and does not let go until the crowd thins.","Less useful in quiet places, where she has nothing to steer around.","Leads Eon through a rainy Akihabara and a crowded convention without losing him once."),
P("Matching Charm","e","Support","Small gifts and matching tokens that turn ordinary outings into shared memories.","A joke gift here, a matching keychain there; she always remembers the moment.","Her gifts are sometimes chosen mainly to embarrass him.","The cat-ear headband from Akihabara ends up on Eon’s shelf; matching keychains hang from both their bags.")]},
{cat:"The Soft Side",blurb:"The quiet strengths beneath the bold front.",items:[
P("Crack in the Armour","e","Core","The courage to let someone see her vulnerable side.","She drops the teasing, the nickname and the defences, and says what she feels in plain words.","It frightens her, and she can only do it with someone she truly trusts.","On a snowy January night, calls him ‘Eon’ instead of ‘otaku-kun’ and tells him she likes spending time with him ‘a lot’."),
P("Patient Heart","e","Peak","The resolve to wait, without pressure, for someone she cares about.","She stays close, keeps inviting and keeps teasing, and lets the friendship set its own pace.","Patience is not the same as certainty; some nights she wonders whether he will ever notice.","Chooses friendship over a forced confession and decides that, for now, being by his side is enough.")]}],
relationships:[
{who:"eon",name:"Eon",kind:"Closest friend",text:"A quiet literature student and gamer who lives alone in Nakano and treasures his solo evenings. She calls him ‘otaku-kun’, takes him everywhere, and has quietly fallen for him."},
{who:"yumi",name:"Yumi",kind:"Friend of Eon’s",text:"A cosplayer from Eon’s anime and game club, and the first person to notice that Risa looks at him differently."},
{who:"takashi",name:"Takashi",kind:"Friend of Eon’s",text:"The loud member of Eon’s club, who cannot quite believe Eon is close to someone so ‘campus level’."},
{who:"dorm-friends",name:"Her friends and dorm-mates",kind:"Social circle",text:"A lively crowd who drag her shopping and to mixers, and who would not understand why she prefers a quiet anime night."},
{who:"park-ji-yeon",kind:"Fellow Luminary",text:"Like [[park-ji-yeon|Ji-yeon]], Risa comes from a world without magic; both met Eon as a quiet student and saw something in him that others missed."}],
trivia:["Her first words to Eon were a question about the anime on his phone: ‘…Is that Shield Hero?’","She bought Eon a cat-ear headband as a joke gift on their first outing. It still sits on his shelf.","She cried at a late-night film screening and made Eon promise never to tell anyone.","Her nickname for Eon is ‘otaku-kun’. She dropped it, once, for the most important conversation of the story.","She lives in a noisy dormitory, which is one reason she secretly envies Eon’s quiet apartment.","She is one of the Luminary-tier characters on this wiki, from a world without magic."],
quotes:[["…Is that Shield Hero?","Her first words to Eon, mid-lecture"],["Don’t ghost me, otaku-kun. I know where your class is.","After exchanging messaging IDs"],["Don’t tell anyone I cried, got it?","After a late-night film screening in Shinjuku"],["Good. Because I like hanging out with you. You’re real.","At the Odaiba convention"],["I like spending time with you. A lot.","On a snowy January night"]]
});
EONC.push({
slug:"nova-astra",img:"nova-astra",short:"Nova Astra",color:"#9b7bff",tags:["divine","mage","eon"],epithet:"the Space Goddess of the Void Weave",
name:"Nova Astra",fullName:"Nova Astra, Space Goddess of the Void Weave Realm",
tagline:"A goddess who ruled the void itself came to the Lucid Lantern to see whether even gods could meet their match there, and stayed.",
aliases:["The Space Goddess","Lady of the Void Weave","Star-Warden of the Lantern","Nova"],titles:["Space Goddess of the Void Weave Realm","Star-Warden of the Lucid Lantern","Keeper of the Lantern Observatory"],
race:"Goddess (celestial fox in her full-power form)",age:"Adult; an ancient goddess of uncounted age",height:"212 cm, the tallest resident of the Lucid Lantern",build:"Towering and long-limbed, with an unhurried, faintly lazy grace that hides enormous power",
hair:"Very long and silky, black shading into deep purple, falling past her knees",eyes:"Glowing violet, said to hold the depth of infinite galaxies",
origin:"The Void Weave Realm",affiliation:"The Lucid Lantern and its household",role:"Former sovereign of the Void Weave Realm; Star-Warden, scout and Anchor-keeper of the Lucid Lantern",
sagas:["lantern"],firstSaga:"lantern",status:"Alive; resides aboard the Lucid Lantern by her own choice",
caption:"Nova Astra in her full-power form, standing on rain-slick stone beneath a full moon before a lantern-lit pagoda: silver-white fox ears, long purple-black hair and a black robe trailing starlit veils.",
tier:"t1b",stats:{off:10,def:9,spd:10,mys:9,utl:9,rea:9},
note:"**Placement.** On the Lucid Lantern’s own scale Nova holds the highest grade of any resident, one step above a fellow goddess said to be able to unmake star systems. On raw scale she outstrips anything [[yue-qingwu|Yue Qingwu]] is shown doing. She still ranks second: Qingwu’s power works on the rules behind power (held time, sequence, the concept of strength), while Nova’s vast dominion is confined to one law, space, and her story’s one great contest ends with her conceding to the Lantern’s keeper on his own ground. She sits in a tier of her own, **Transcendent**.",
intro:"**Nova Astra** is the Space Goddess of the Void Weave Realm: a 212-centimetre goddess with purple-black hair and galaxy-violet eyes, who once commanded space itself. In her everyday form she looks like a striking, slightly lazy beauty. When she releases her full power she becomes a regal goddess in a robe of night and starlight, with celestial fox ears and glowing markings. Drawn by rumours of the Lucid Lantern, a dream-restaurant that drifts between realities and is said to be the place where even gods find their match, she arrives to test them herself. Three days later she asks to stay. She becomes the Lantern’s Star-Warden: its scout among the stars, keeper of its Anchors and the quiet watcher in its observatory.",
bio:[
{h:"Sovereign of the void",t:"Before the Lantern, Nova ruled the Void Weave Realm, a domain of open space, folded distance and slow-turning stars. ‘The void used to be mine,’ she later says. ‘I commanded space itself.’ It was a vast and silent kingdom, and by her own account a lonely one: she had everything a goddess could want and felt, at the end of it, empty.\n\nRumours eventually reached even the void: somewhere among the dream-realms drifted a floating restaurant of golden lanterns, kept by a traveller called the Lucid Dreamer, where proud gods and sovereigns who came to test him found their match."},
{h:"The Lucid Lantern",t:"The Lantern is a many-storeyed hall of warm light and floating lanterns that drifts through nebulae, quiet voids and gentle dream-realms. Its keeper is Eon, who sits behind the counter in an oversized chair and greets every guest the same way. Its household is unusual. There is Feng Lian, an Empress of the Celestial Dream Pagoda Continent and Eon’s wife, who visits through a blooming lotus portal with their daughter Luminara, a brilliant young Dream Angel. There is Elizabeth, a former Outer Goddess with pink-silver hair, who was once a terror of her realm. There is Zeiss, a former Thunder Sovereign who once stormed a heaven of gods and now runs the Lantern as its Store Manager. And there is Lirael Sylvaine, a graceful former High Arbiter who spent centuries mediating between gods."},
{h:"The Space Goddess’s arrival",t:"One peaceful evening the Lantern’s doors open in a shimmering ripple of starlight. The woman who steps through is taller than anyone in the hall and wrapped in an aura of quiet, overwhelming power. Eon, who has welcomed thunder sovereigns and outer goddesses, recognises at once that this guest may be the strongest yet.\n\nShe scans the hall with a faint, intrigued smile. ‘So this is the place where even gods find their match,’ she says, in a voice like distant stars colliding. ‘I have come to see if the rumours are true.’ Eon calmly offers her the Lantern’s challenge. Her violet eyes spark. ‘Then I accept. But I will not yield easily.’"},
{h:"Three days",t:"What follows is a contest of wills fought on the Lantern’s own ground, where the Lucid Dreamer’s rules hold. Nova arrives intending, as she later admits, to conquer the place. For three Lantern days she presses the full weight of the void against a hall that simply refuses to fold.\n\nAt the end of it she does not leave. ‘When I first arrived, I thought I was going to conquer this place,’ she tells the household, laughing. ‘Three days later I was asking to stay.’ Eon welcomes her into the household, and the once-proud goddess finds that losing, here, feels far more like coming home than winning ever did."},
{h:"Star-Warden",t:"Nova settles into the Lantern with surprising ease. In quiet stretches with no guests she is the one curled up beside Eon with a book of star charts, or laughing at Zeiss’s attempts to give a serious manager’s report. Her power grows rather than fades: her command of space becomes so refined that she helps stabilise the Lantern’s new Anchors, the portal-links that let travellers come and go safely, and she scouts the passing realities for worthy goddesses who might one day find their way to its light.\n\nWhen the household compares their old lives, she is candid. ‘I used to command the void itself. Now I’m happiest when I’m simply here. It’s strangely liberating.’"},
{h:"The offer of freedom",t:"One evening Eon asks a question that unsettles the whole household: what if he gave each of them real freedom, to go anywhere in the outside worlds for as long as they wished, with no Anchor drawing them back?\n\nNova wraps her long arms around him and answers without hesitation. ‘The void used to be mine. I commanded space itself. But nothing compared to being here. If you set me free, I would spend every moment trying to find my way back to you.’ Feng Lian speaks for everyone: they have all chosen this. Eon does not raise the question again."},
{h:"The observatory",t:"Later, Eon asks each resident for a wish of her own. Nova’s is small: ‘a little observatory room where I can watch the stars and realities we pass through. It would help me scout better.’ Then, more softly, she adds that the only thing she truly wants is to stay. Eon grants it, and the Lantern grows a domed observatory where Nova spends long hours watching nebulae and dream-realms drift past.\n\nAt the same time, Eon gives every resident a gift shaped to her nature. Nova’s is a band of black and purple, swirling with galaxy patterns and tiny glowing stars. She wears it proudly as a sign that she belongs to the Lantern’s family."},
{h:"Watching Luminara",t:"When Eon suggests that his daughter Luminara try exploring other worlds, every resident offers help. Nova’s offer is the most practical: ‘I can scout space-related worlds for her if needed.’ Through a dream-crystal mirror, the household watches Luminara’s first expedition live, to a sky archipelago of floating islands, vine bridges and floating academies.\n\nAs Luminara calms a crystalline dragon with a net of dream-light, Nova nods: ‘Her cosmic awareness is growing. She’s adapting so quickly.’ When Luminara is pushed to her limit by a rift-beast and wins, Nova holds on to Eon a little tighter: ‘She’s making us all proud.’ On a second journey Luminara turns a battle into a musical and heals a world-rift into a floating garden, and Nova grins: ‘Her imagination is becoming truly cosmic.’ Each time Luminara returns, Nova is part of the group hug that meets her at the portal."}],
appearance:"Nova is the tallest resident of the Lucid Lantern at 212 centimetres, with long, elegant legs and an unhurried posture that makes even her stillness look deliberate. Her silky hair falls past her knees, black at the roots and shading into deep purple, often shot through with faint violet sparks. Her eyes glow violet and seem to hold whole galaxies. Her skin carries a soft cosmic glow.\n\nShe has two forms. In her everyday form she dresses simply, in casual black clothes, and looks like a striking, faintly lazy beauty who has wandered in from a city street. In her full-power form she becomes a regal goddess: fox ears rise from her hair, celestial markings glow along her skin and she is robed in layered black silk embroidered with silver star-chains, veiled in sheets of translucent, starlit blue that drift around her like a nebula.\n\nThe portrait shows her full-length in that full-power form, standing on rain-slick stone beneath a full moon before a lantern-lit pagoda: silver-white fox ears rise from her purple-black hair, violet eyes glow beneath a dark fringe, silver chains and amethyst drops hang from her hair ornaments, and her black robe with silver embroidery and starlit veils pools at her feet. After the observatory evening she also wears a black-and-purple band patterned with swirling galaxies and tiny glowing stars.",
personality:[
{h:"Proud and challenging",t:"Nova arrives at the Lantern as a goddess who has never met her equal, and it shows: an intrigued half-smile, a calm voice, a challenge accepted before it is fully offered. ‘I will not yield easily.’ She still enjoys a contest and, when the household competes, declares that as the newest arrival she has something to prove."},
{h:"Lazy grace",t:"Outside a fight she is relaxed to the point of languor. She lounges, she laughs easily and she finds the household’s rivalries funny. ‘You’re all so competitive,’ she says, from wherever she happens to be comfortable."},
{h:"Candid and warm",t:"Nova is disarmingly honest about her past: she ruled the void, felt empty and is happier now. She gives praise freely, especially to Luminara, and is quick to join a group hug."},
{h:"Devoted by choice",t:"Her loyalty to Eon and the Lantern is something she chose with her eyes open, and she is firm about it: offered her freedom, she refuses it outright. Being asked to leave would feel to her like being told she is not wanted."},
{h:"Fears",t:"Having once had everything and felt nothing, she fears that emptiness above all, and being sent away from the only place that ever filled it."}],
powersIntro:"Nova is a goddess of space. The story states her dominion (she commanded the void of an entire realm) and grades her the highest of all the Lantern’s residents, one step above a goddess who could casually destroy star systems, but it shows most of that power only in passing. The powers below are drawn from what she is said and seen to do, with names coined for this wiki except where marked; where a power’s scale is inferred from her grade rather than shown, the entry says so.",
powers:[
{cat:"Sovereignty of the Void Weave",blurb:"The dominion she held before the Lantern.",items:[
P("Dominion of the Void Weave","e","Beyond","Sovereign command over the space of an entire realm: distance, direction, emptiness and the paths between stars.","Space answers her will as a native law of her being; she does not cast it so much as decide it.","Its full reach applies in her own realm; inside the Lantern, where the Dreamer’s rules hold, it is checked.","Stated in her own words: ‘The void used to be mine. I commanded space itself.’"),
P("Starbreaker Scale","e","Beyond","Destructive capability on the scale of whole star systems.","The void folds and collapses on command; the energy involved is cosmic rather than merely planetary.","Inferred, not shown: she never releases it in the chronicle, and she has no wish to.","Graded above a fellow resident who ‘could casually destroy star systems’."),
P("Aura of the Quiet Void","e","Peak","A silent, overwhelming pressure that tells everyone in a room exactly how strong she is.","Her presence leaks the weight of the void into the air around her.","She can hold it in; it is simply her default.","Enters the Lantern ‘with an aura of quiet, overwhelming power’; its keeper judges her perhaps the strongest guest yet.")]},
{cat:"Spatial Arts",blurb:"The working tools of a goddess of space.",items:[
P("Starlight Threshold","e","Core","Opens a passage through space and steps out of it wrapped in starlight.","She parts the space between two points like a curtain.","Leaves a visible ripple of light; it is not a stealthy entrance.","Arrives at the Lucid Lantern’s doors in a shimmering ripple of starlight."),
P("Fold of Distance","e","Core","Brings far places near: crossing vast distances in a single step, or bringing a distant object to hand.","Space between departure and arrival is folded flat, so no distance is actually travelled.","Requires a sense of the destination; unknown places must first be scouted.","Implied by her rule of the void and her role as the Lantern’s scout of distant realities."),
P("Gravity Well","e","Peak","Compresses space around a target until it cannot move, or pulls a whole field of objects toward a single point.","She curves the space itself rather than pushing the object.","Precise use at small scales takes concentration; at large scales it is anything but gentle.","Editor’s name for the crushing side of her space command; held in reserve during her stay."),
P("Hollow Pocket","e","Support","Creates small sealed pockets of space for storage, shelter or safekeeping.","Space is woven into a closed loop that opens only for her.","Pockets are small and must be maintained.","Editor’s extension of her command of space; not shown directly in the chronicle."),
P("Anchor-Weaving","s","Core","Stabilises the Anchors, the portal-links that let travellers move safely between the Lantern and other worlds.","She steadies the space at each end of the link so the portal does not drift or tear.","Collaborative work: it builds on the Lantern’s own dream-structure.","Her space-manipulation grows ‘tremendously’ aboard the Lantern, ‘allowing her to help stabilise new Anchors’.")]},
{cat:"Celestial Fox Ascension",blurb:"Her full-power form.",items:[
P("Robe of the Night Sky","e","Peak","Her full-power transformation: fox ears, glowing celestial markings and a regal robe of night-black silk and starlit veils.","She releases the restraint of her everyday form and lets her divinity show.","She rarely needs it, and prefers to lounge in her casual form.","When she releases her full power she transforms into a regal goddess ‘radiating divine authority’."),
P("Divine Authority","e","Peak","A presence in her full-power form that commands deference from lesser powers.","The weight of a sovereign goddess made visible.","Commands respect, not obedience; it does not work on the Lantern’s keeper.","Described as radiating divine authority in her ascended form."),
P("Voice of Colliding Stars","e","Support","A resonant voice that carries through any hall without being raised.","Each word is pitched with the quiet resonance of distant stars.","Purely a matter of presence; it compels nobody.","Her first words in the Lantern carry to every corner of the hall.")]},
{cat:"Star-Warden of the Lantern",blurb:"The duties she chose aboard the Lucid Lantern.",items:[
P("Cosmic Senses","s","Core","Perceives the shape, energy and nature of distant worlds and beings across space.","She reads the ‘space’ of a world, a realm or a person the way others read weather.","Works best on places with strong spatial or celestial character.","Scouts potential new worlds for the household ‘using her cosmic senses’, and reads Luminara’s growing cosmic awareness from afar."),
P("Observatory of Passing Realities","s","Utility","A domed observatory aboard the Lantern from which she watches the stars and realities the hall drifts through.","Her wish, granted by Eon; she pairs it with her cosmic senses to map what lies ahead.","A place, not a weapon; it is only as useful as the eyes that watch from it.","‘A little observatory room where I can watch the stars and realities we pass through. It would help me scout better.’"),
P("Worthy-Soul Scouting","s","Support","Finds goddesses and travellers worthy of the Lantern’s light among the infinite realities.","Combines cosmic senses, patience and long nights in the observatory.","Scouts, never compels; whether a guest comes is up to them.","Helps ‘recruit worthy goddesses’ alongside the Store Manager."),
P("Explorer’s Pathfinding","s","Support","Charts safe routes through space-related worlds for travellers setting out from the Lantern.","Surveys a destination’s spatial currents before anyone steps through.","Most useful for worlds with strong spatial energies.","‘I can scout space-related worlds for her if needed,’ she promises Luminara before her first expedition.")]},
{cat:"The Galaxy Within",blurb:"Gifts that come simply from what she is.",items:[
P("Galaxy-Deep Gaze","e","Support","Eyes that take in the true measure of whatever they rest on.","The galaxies in her violet eyes are not only decoration; she sees depth.","Measures strength and growth, not intentions.","Judges the Lantern worth testing at a glance, and later spots Luminara’s growth through a dream-mirror."),
P("Ever-Growing Expanse","e","Peak","Her power keeps growing rather than settling, the way space itself expands.","Use and purpose refine her command; the Lantern gives both.","Growth is gradual and depends on what she spends it on.","Her space-manipulation powers grow ‘tremendously’ after she joins the household.")]}],
relationships:[
{who:"eon",name:"Eon",kind:"Partner; keeper of the Lantern",text:"The Lucid Dreamer behind the Lantern’s counter. She came to test him, met her match, and has refused every offer to leave."},
{who:"feng-lian",name:"Feng Lian",kind:"Lady of the household",text:"An Empress of the Celestial Dream Pagoda Continent and Eon’s wife, who speaks for the whole household when Eon offers them freedom: ‘We’ve all chosen this.’"},
{who:"luminara",name:"Luminara",kind:"Eon’s daughter",text:"A brilliant young Dream Angel and scholar. Nova scouts worlds for her expeditions and is one of her proudest watchers."},
{who:"zeiss",name:"Zeiss",kind:"Fellow resident",text:"A former Thunder Sovereign turned the Lantern’s Store Manager, with whom Nova scouts for new arrivals."},
{who:"elizabeth",name:"Elizabeth",kind:"Fellow resident",text:"A former Outer Goddess with pink-silver hair, the Lantern’s first resident and one grade below Nova on its scale."},
{who:"lirael-sylvaine",name:"Lirael Sylvaine",kind:"Fellow resident",text:"A graceful former High Arbiter who keeps the Lantern’s peace (no relation to [[lirael-kanto|Lirael Kanto]])."},
{who:"yue-qingwu",kind:"Rival for the top of the ranking",text:"[[yue-qingwu|Yue Qingwu]] outranks Nova on this wiki: Nova’s dominion is greater in raw scale, but Qingwu’s power reaches the rules behind power itself."}],
trivia:["At 212 cm she is the tallest resident of the Lucid Lantern.","Her own summary of her arrival: she came to conquer the place, and three days later asked to stay.","Her only personal wish was an observatory; her real wish, she said, was simply to stay.","On the Lantern’s scale she holds its highest grade, one step above a goddess said to be able to unmake star systems.","She is second in this wiki’s Power Ranking, behind Yue Qingwu and ahead of Lirael Kanto, and the only character in the Transcendent tier.","Her full-power form has fox ears and celestial markings; her everyday form has neither."],
quotes:[["So this is the place where even gods find their match. I have come to see if the rumours are true.","On entering the Lucid Lantern"],["Then I accept. But I will not yield easily.","Accepting the Lantern’s challenge"],["The void used to be mine. I commanded space itself. If you set me free, I would spend every moment trying to find my way back to you.","Refusing Eon’s offer of freedom"],["Her imagination is becoming truly cosmic.","Watching Luminara’s second expedition"],["You’re all so competitive.","To the household"]]
});
EONC.push({
slug:"nakamura-hana",img:"nakamura-hana",short:"Nakamura Hana",color:"#c79ad8",tags:["eon"],epithet:"the sheltered Kyoto heiress promised to a Tokyo heir",
name:"Nakamura Hana",fullName:"Nakamura Hana (Hana Nakamura in Western name order)",
tagline:"Raised behind the gates of a strict Kyoto academy, she came to Tokyo to meet the young man their mothers had chosen, and chose him herself.",
aliases:["Hana","Hana-san","The Nakamura Heiress","Little Kyoto (Eon’s teasing name)"],titles:["Heiress of the Nakamura shipping house","Fiancée of the Takahashi heir","First-year university student"],
race:"Human",age:"19 (adult); two years younger than Eon",height:"Not specified; slender and of average height",build:"Slight and graceful, with the upright posture of years of etiquette lessons",
hair:"Long, straight and black, with soft full bangs",eyes:"Large, gentle grey-brown eyes",
origin:"Kyoto, Japan",affiliation:"The Nakamura family (shipping); by engagement, the Takahashi family (semiconductors)",role:"University student; heiress; Eon’s fiancée",
sagas:["kyoto"],firstSaga:"kyoto",status:"Alive; engaged to Eon, the wedding planned for after both graduate",
caption:"Nakamura Hana standing barefoot against a dark studio backdrop, in a white top and black shorts, long black hair with soft bangs and a gentle, shy expression.",
tier:"t7",stats:{off:1,def:2,spd:2,mys:3,utl:8,rea:2},
note:"**A world without magic.** Hana’s chronicle is a modern family story of Tokyo and Kyoto with no spells, gods or systems. She joins the **Luminary** tier, and her ‘powers’ are the accomplishments of a young woman raised by private tutors and an exacting academy: etiquette, calligraphy, music, a scholar’s memory, and a quiet resolve that surprises everyone, herself included.",
intro:"**Nakamura Hana** is the nineteen-year-old daughter of Mrs. Nakamura, head of a great shipping house. From the age of six she was educated at an ultra-strict all-girls academy in Kyoto and by private tutors, and she grew up sweet, kind, impeccably mannered and almost entirely sheltered. Her mother’s oldest friend is the mother of **Eon**, the twenty-one-year-old university student who is heir to the Takahashi family’s semiconductor business in Tokyo, and the two mothers have a plan: an engagement by the end of the year, a wedding once both have finished university, and two great families joined. Hana is told about the arrangement, and to everyone’s surprise she is excited. Her chronicle follows what happens when an arranged promise slowly becomes a real one.",
bio:[
{h:"Behind the academy gates",t:"Hana grew up in the Nakamura family’s Kyoto residence and, from the age of six, behind the gates of an ultra-strict all-girls academy where bells marked every hour and a crooked bow was corrected on the spot. Private tutors filled the time the academy did not: calligraphy, the koto, tea ceremony, classical literature and languages.\n\nShe emerged at nineteen accomplished, polite to a fault, and almost entirely unacquainted with ordinary life. She had never ridden a train alone, never bought anything at a convenience store and never spent an afternoon with a young man her own age. She was also, everyone agreed, the kindest girl in her year."},
{h:"Two mothers and a plan",t:"Mrs. Nakamura, who runs the family’s shipping empire, and Mrs. Takahashi, whose family leads a major semiconductor company in Tokyo, have been friends for years. Over tea one spring they decide that their children should meet. If all goes well there will be an engagement before the year is out and a wedding once both have finished university, binding the two houses together.\n\nEon, the Takahashi heir, is a calm twenty-one-year-old university student who agrees, cautiously, to a first meeting and nothing more. The message that comes back from Kyoto surprises him: Hana is excited to meet him."},
{h:"A first meeting in the garden",t:"They meet in the tea room of the Takahashi family’s Tokyo residence, looking out on a spring garden. Hana arrives in a pale kimono, bows so perfectly that Eon feels obliged to bow again, and then, once the two mothers have discreetly withdrawn to admire the koi, asks him a long list of earnest questions she has clearly prepared in advance. What does he study? What does a semiconductor actually do? Is it true that people in Tokyo eat while walking?\n\nEon, who had expected a stiff formality, finds himself laughing. Before they part, Hana confides in a small voice that she has never taken a train by herself. He offers to show her how."},
{h:"Tokyo for the first time",t:"That April Hana moves to Tokyo to begin her first year at university, staying at the Nakamura family’s city residence, and Eon keeps his promise. Her first commuter card is a small triumph. Her first convenience store is a revelation: she studies the rice-ball wrappers with scholarly attention and buys one of everything. She stops in the middle of the Shibuya scramble, enchanted, until Eon gently steers her across. She discovers crepes, rainy-day bookshops, arcades (where she is hopeless) and the simple pleasure of getting slightly lost.\n\nEvery new thing delights her, and Eon begins to see his own city through her eyes. Things he has walked past a thousand times become, beside her, worth stopping for."},
{h:"Brush, strings and circuits",t:"They trade worlds. Eon takes Hana on a visitor’s tour of the Takahashi company’s showroom and laboratories, and she listens to engineers explain chip design with such rapt attention that they keep talking long after the tour should have ended. In return she sits him down with brush and ink and teaches him to write a single character. He writes it badly; she frames it anyway.\n\nOn a summer evening she plays the koto for him. The piece is one she has played since childhood, but she tells him afterwards it is the first time she has played it for someone rather than for an examiner."},
{h:"Kyoto in summer",t:"In July Hana takes Eon to her Kyoto. They walk the banks of the Kamo River at dusk, watch the lantern-lit floats of the summer festival and stop outside the gates of her old academy, where a stern former teacher recognises her and, unexpectedly, smiles.\n\nSitting by the river, Hana tells him something she has never said aloud: that every important thing in her life has been chosen for her, and that she has always wondered what it would feel like to choose something herself."},
{h:"The question under the maples",t:"In autumn Hana overhears two relatives talking about the engagement as a merger, a sensible union of shipping and semiconductors. For the first time she wonders whether Eon agreed only out of duty. For days she says nothing. Then, beneath the illuminated maples of a Tokyo garden, the girl who was taught never to ask awkward questions asks him directly.\n\nEon tells her the truth: that he came to the first meeting because his mother asked him to, and that every meeting since has been his own choice. If there were no arrangement at all, he says, he would still be standing exactly here. Hana is quiet for a long moment. Then she tells him that she chose too, the day he offered to teach her to ride a train."},
{h:"A promise made real",t:"On a snowy evening at the end of December, the engagement is formalised at the Takahashi residence with both families present. The two mothers are delighted and make no effort to hide it. Eon gives Hana a ring; Hana gives Eon a scroll she has written herself, a single character meaning *bond*, in her finest brushwork. The wedding is set for after both have graduated.\n\nOn New Year’s morning they make their first shrine visit of the year together. Hana writes her wish on a wooden plaque and refuses, laughing, to let him read it. The arrangement their mothers made in spring has become something neither family arranged: a promise the two of them chose."}],
appearance:"Hana is slender and graceful, with the straight-backed poise of a girl who has spent thirteen years being corrected on posture. Her long black hair falls straight past her shoulders, with soft, full bangs that frame large, gentle grey-brown eyes. Her complexion is fair, and she blushes easily, especially when she is complimented.\n\nThe portrait shows her full-length, standing barefoot against a dark backdrop in a white top and black shorts: long black hair with soft bangs, a shy, thoughtful expression and a faint blush.\n\nFor formal occasions, such as the first meeting and the engagement, she wears a pale kimono. Day to day in Tokyo she favours simple, soft-coloured clothes, such as a cream top, and carries a small notebook in which she writes down every new thing she learns about the city.",
personality:[
{h:"Sweet and kind",t:"Hana’s kindness is the first thing anyone notices and the last thing they forget. She thanks every shop assistant, remembers the names of the Takahashi household staff after one introduction and worries more about other people’s comfort than her own."},
{h:"Innocent and endlessly curious",t:"Sheltered all her life, she meets ordinary things with genuine wonder: trains, convenience stores, arcade games, street food. She asks questions constantly, without embarrassment, and remembers every answer."},
{h:"Perfectly mannered",t:"Her etiquette is flawless and occasionally comic: she bows to vending machines when flustered and apologises to doors she bumps into. She is slowly learning that not every moment requires formality."},
{h:"Quietly resolute",t:"Behind the gentleness is a surprising firmness. When something truly matters she will ask the difficult question, hold her ground or make her own choice, softly but without wavering."},
{h:"Fears",t:"Her deepest fear is being loved only as a duty: being, as she once puts it, ‘a sensible arrangement’ rather than a person. She also worries, endearingly, about getting lost on the Tokyo subway."}],
powersIntro:"Hana has no magic. What she has is the discipline of a strict Kyoto academy, the accomplishments of years of private tutoring, a sheltered girl’s gift for wonder and a quiet strength that only shows when it is needed. Every name below was coined for this wiki.",
powers:[
{cat:"Kyoto Grace",blurb:"Thirteen years of the strictest etiquette in Japan.",items:[
P("The Perfect Bow","e","Core","Etiquette so precise it sets the tone of any room she enters.","Thirteen years of daily correction at the academy; every angle and pause is exact.","Can make casual company feel overdressed, until her smile puts them at ease.","Bows so perfectly at the first meeting that Eon instinctively bows a second time."),
P("Tea-Room Stillness","e","Support","A calm, unhurried composure drawn from the tea ceremony, which steadies those around her.","She slows her breath and movements as if preparing tea, and the room follows.","Harder to summon when she is flustered, which in Tokyo is often.","Keeps a nervous first meeting gentle and unhurried once the mothers have left the room."),
P("Kimono Poise","e","Support","Moves with complete ease and grace in formal kimono.","Years of practice in the academy’s formal ceremonies.","Purely a matter of grace; it helps not at all on a crowded train.","Glides through the first meeting and the engagement evening without a misstep.")]},
{cat:"Brush & Strings",blurb:"The arts her tutors gave her.",items:[
P("Brush of One Breath","e","Peak","Calligraphy of near-professional quality, each character written in a single unbroken breath.","Ink, posture and breath aligned; she never retouches a stroke.","Needs quiet and time; she cannot rush it.","Writes the scroll bearing the character for *bond* that she gives Eon at their engagement."),
P("Falling-Petal Koto","e","Peak","Music on the koto that can hold a room in silence.","Childhood training with private tutors, refined for performance and examination.","She plays best for someone, not for an audience, a discovery she makes during the chronicle.","Plays for Eon on a summer evening, the first time she has played for a person rather than an examiner."),
P("Classical Memory","e","Support","An extensive memory of classical literature, poetry and languages.","Years of private tutoring and recitation.","Book knowledge; it does not help her read a Tokyo subway map.","Recites poems to match every season and place they visit.")]},
{cat:"Sheltered Wonder",blurb:"The gifts of seeing everything for the first time.",items:[
P("First-Time Eyes","e","Core","A delight in ordinary things so genuine that it makes others see them anew.","She notices everything and enjoys it openly, without irony.","It can make her late; there is always something worth stopping for.","Stops in the middle of the Shibuya scramble, enchanted, and leaves Eon seeing his own city differently."),
P("The Earnest Question","e","Core","Disarming sincerity: her questions are so honest that people answer them honestly.","She prepares her questions carefully and asks them without guile.","Occasionally asks things others would consider too direct.","Turns a stiff formal meeting into laughter with a prepared list of questions about semiconductors and walking while eating."),
P("Quick Study","e","Support","Learns new skills and environments remarkably fast.","Academy discipline applied to everyday life: notes, practice and review.","Arcade games remain the one exception.","Masters the Tokyo rail network within weeks of her first solo journey.")]},
{cat:"Quiet Resolve",blurb:"The strength nobody expected from her.",items:[
P("Unbending Bamboo","e","Peak","A quiet resolve that, once roused, does not give way.","She bends politely in small things and does not bend at all in large ones.","Takes time to rouse; she prefers harmony.","Asks Eon directly, under the autumn maples, whether he agreed to the engagement only out of duty."),
P("A Choice of Her Own","e","Core","The courage to choose for herself in a life where most things were chosen for her.","She weighs the matter quietly, then commits completely.","She worries that wanting something for herself is selfish, and has to be reminded it is not.","Tells Eon she chose him the day he offered to teach her to ride a train."),
P("Gentle Heart","e","Support","A warmth that makes everyone around her feel cared for.","Small, constant kindnesses: thanks, remembered names, quiet help.","Sometimes forgets to look after herself.","Wins over the Takahashi household staff, and a stern old teacher at her academy gates, simply by being herself.")]}],
relationships:[
{who:"eon",name:"Eon",kind:"Fiancé",text:"The calm twenty-one-year-old heir of the Takahashi semiconductor family, who agreed to meet her as a favour to his mother and stayed by his own choice."},
{who:"mrs-nakamura",name:"Mrs. Nakamura",kind:"Mother",text:"Head of the Nakamura shipping empire, who arranged the first meeting with her oldest friend and is delighted with how it turned out."},
{who:"mrs-takahashi",name:"Mrs. Takahashi",kind:"Future mother-in-law",text:"Eon’s mother and Mrs. Nakamura’s longtime friend, the other half of the matchmaking plan, who welcomes Hana warmly."},
{who:"academy-teacher",name:"Her former teacher",kind:"Mentor",text:"A stern instructor at the Kyoto academy who once corrected every bow Hana made, and smiles to see her again."},
{who:"hamazaki-risa",kind:"Fellow Luminary",text:"[[hamazaki-risa|Risa]] and Hana both live in a modern Tokyo without magic, one a bold campus gal and one a sheltered Kyoto heiress."},
{who:"park-ji-yeon",kind:"Fellow Luminary",text:"Like [[park-ji-yeon|Ji-yeon]], Hana is joined to an heir whose family fortune she never cared about."}],
trivia:["She had never ridden a train by herself before coming to Tokyo.","At her first convenience store she bought one of every kind of rice ball, to compare.","Her engagement gift to Eon was a scroll with the character for *bond*, written in a single breath.","Eon’s first attempt at calligraphy, under her tuition, hangs framed in her room.","She wrote a wish at the New Year shrine visit and has never told Eon what it said.","She is one of the Luminary-tier characters on this wiki, from a world without magic."],
quotes:[["Is it true that people in Tokyo eat while they walk?","One of her prepared questions at the first meeting"],["I have never taken a train by myself.","Confiding in Eon in the garden"],["Every important thing in my life was chosen for me. I always wondered what it would feel like to choose something myself.","By the Kamo River in summer"],["I chose too. The day you offered to teach me to ride a train.","Under the autumn maples"],["You may not read it. Not yet.","On her New Year wish"]]
});
EONC.push({
slug:"arisugawa-yu",img:"arisugawa-yu",short:"Arisugawa Yu",color:"#8e5fb8",tags:["leader","eon"],epithet:"the silk-gowned matriarch of Tokyo high society who chose Eon’s household as her own",
name:"Arisugawa Yu",fullName:"Arisugawa Yu (有栖川 悠; Chinese name Yu Wanqing, 余婉清)",
tagline:"She owned the view from the forty-eighth floor, ran a house older than most of Tokyo’s towers, and had long since stopped expecting anyone to surprise her. Then a university student corrected her tea.",
aliases:["Yu","Yu-sama (household staff)","Madam Arisugawa","The Lady of the Forty-Eighth Floor","Wanqing (to her late grandmother)","The Purple Peony (society columns)"],
titles:["Head of the Arisugawa house","Chairwoman of Arisugawa Holdings","Patroness of the Tokyo–Shanghai Cultural Foundation","Eon’s business partner and confidante","Matriarch of the Takahashi heir’s household"],
race:"Human",age:"Early to mid forties (adult)",height:"About 168 cm",build:"Tall, slender and statuesque, with a dancer’s carriage",
hair:"Very long, glossy black hair, usually swept up and pinned with gold and pearl ornaments",eyes:"Dark amber eyes with a slight, knowing tilt",
origin:"Tokyo, Japan; her mother’s family is from Suzhou, China",affiliation:"The Arisugawa house and Arisugawa Holdings; by choice, the household of Eon of the Takahashi family",
role:"Businesswoman, society hostess and patroness of the arts; Eon’s partner in business and his household’s matriarch",
sagas:["peony"],firstSaga:"peony",status:"Alive; lives in Eon’s household and still keeps her penthouse ‘for the view’",
caption:"Arisugawa Yu seated on a sofa in her penthouse at night, in a purple silk gown embroidered with flowers, long black hair pinned with ornaments, with the Tokyo skyline glittering through the windows behind her.",
tier:"t7",stats:{off:2,def:5,spd:3,mys:4,utl:10,rea:4},
note:"**A world without magic.** Yu belongs to the same modern Tokyo as [[nakamura-hana|Nakamura Hana]]: no spells, gods or systems. She joins the **Luminary** tier, and her ‘powers’ are the talents of a woman who has run an old house and a modern company for twenty years: negotiation, social command, two languages and two cultures, the tea table, the silk gown and a presence that society columnists describe, not entirely jokingly, as a weather system. One of them, her famous ‘read’ of people, is so uncanny that it is listed here as a light mystique, but it is never more than very sharp eyes.",
intro:"**Arisugawa Yu** is the head of the old Arisugawa house and chairwoman of Arisugawa Holdings, a Tokyo group in real estate, luxury hotels and Japan–China trade. Daughter of a Japanese father and a mother from a Suzhou family of silk merchants and scholars, she grew up between two languages and two etiquettes and mastered both. She inherited the family business young, in a crisis, and spent two decades making it formidable. By her forties she had everything Tokyo can offer and, privately, very little she still wanted. Then, at a charity tea she was hosting, she met **Eon**, a calm twenty-one-year-old university student and heir to the Takahashi semiconductor family, who was not impressed by her in the slightest and said so politely. Her chronicle follows how two adults from very different stages of life became business partners, then each other’s most trusted confidant, and how a woman who had always lived alone at the top of a tower chose, at last, to come down and make a home in his.",
bio:[
{h:"Two cities in one cradle",t:"Yu was born in Tokyo to Arisugawa Kazuhiro, heir to an old merchant house, and Yu Meilan, the daughter of a Suzhou family of silk traders and calligraphers. Her Japanese name and her Chinese one were chosen together, and she answered to both. She spent school years in Tokyo and long summers in her grandmother’s garden house in Suzhou, learning Chinese brush painting, the guqin and gongfu tea at one end of the year and Japanese tea ceremony, ikebana and the iron etiquette of an old Tokyo family at the other.\n\nHer grandmother taught her the lesson she would repeat for the rest of her life: *a lady never raises her voice, because she never needs to.*"},
{h:"The crisis year",t:"Yu was twenty-four and studying finance abroad when her father fell seriously ill and a hostile group of investors moved to break up Arisugawa Holdings while the house was leaderless. She flew home, walked into a board meeting that had already decided to sell, and asked for one hour.\n\nWhat she did with that hour became a Tokyo business legend. She had read every contract overnight, found the clause the investors had overlooked, and called, in fluent Mandarin, three Shanghai partners who had known her mother since childhood. By the end of the hour the sale was dead and the group had a new chairwoman. The newspapers called her ‘the girl who saved the house in sixty minutes’. She disliked the nickname and never once corrected it."},
{h:"The lady of the forty-eighth floor",t:"Over the next twenty years Yu rebuilt the company into one of the most respected groups in Tokyo: luxury hotels known for their quiet perfection, real estate in the city’s best districts, and a trade bridge between Japan and China that rival firms could never quite copy, because it ran on personal trust she had spent years earning.\n\nShe lives in a penthouse on the forty-eighth floor of an Arisugawa tower, with floor-to-ceiling windows that look across the whole lit skyline. She hosts the most sought-after salons in the city. She is on friendly terms with the great families, including Mrs. Nakamura of the shipping house, with whom she sits on two charity boards. And she has lived for years, by choice and then by habit, entirely alone. Her friends say she is the most admired woman in Tokyo. Her closest friend once told her, more honestly, that she seemed bored."},
{h:"A charity tea and an honest guest",t:"The chronicle opens at the Arisugawa Foundation’s autumn charity tea, where Yu personally prepares tea for a table of guests. One of them is **Eon**, twenty-one, attending in place of his mother, Mrs. Takahashi. Everyone at the table praises Yu’s tea extravagantly. Eon tastes it, thinks, and says quietly that the water was a little too hot for that leaf, and that she seems to have been distracted while pouring.\n\nThe table falls silent. Yu studies him for a long moment, then laughs, the first real laugh anyone at the Foundation has heard from her in years. He is right: she had been thinking about a contract. She invites him to come back the following week and taste it properly."},
{h:"The student and the chairwoman",t:"Eon does come back, and keeps coming. Yu discovers that he is calm, observant, utterly unbothered by her reputation and genuinely interested in how things work, whether a hotel, a trade route or a tea leaf. He discovers that the most intimidating woman in Tokyo is, in private, dryly funny, endlessly curious and a little lonely.\n\nTheir conversations range from Song-dynasty poetry to semiconductor supply chains. She begins asking his opinion on business matters, half as a test. When his casual remark about a factory’s power costs saves one of her projects a fortune, she stops testing him and starts listening."},
{h:"The Shanghai negotiation",t:"In winter a major Shanghai partner threatens to walk away from the Arisugawa trade bridge, and Yu asks Eon to come with her as an adviser, partly because the deal touches semiconductors and partly, she admits later, because she wanted him to see her work.\n\nHe sees her at her best: switching between Japanese and Mandarin mid-sentence, reading the room before anyone speaks, turning a hostile dinner into a toast. He also sees the moment she nearly loses, when the partner insults her mother’s family, and the iron calm with which she wins anyway. On the night flight home she falls asleep against the window, and he quietly covers her with his coat. When she wakes she says nothing about it, but she keeps the coat for a week."},
{h:"Partners",t:"In spring Yu offers Eon something no one expected: a formal partnership between Arisugawa Holdings and a new venture of his own, joining her hotels and trade network with the Takahashi family’s technology. The press calls it a merger of old money and new; Yu calls it ‘the first investment in years I made because I wanted to’.\n\nThe partnership works. More importantly, the two of them become each other’s most trusted confidant. She is the person he talks to about the weight of being an heir; he is the only person in Tokyo who tells her when she is tired, and makes her stop."},
{h:"A home instead of a view",t:"The turning point comes on a stormy summer night when the power fails across her tower and Yu, alone in the dark at the top of forty-eight floors, finds herself calling Eon without quite knowing why. He arrives with candles and convenience-store dinners, and they sit on the floor of her penthouse watching lightning over the city.\n\nShe tells him that she has spent twenty years building a beautiful view and has nobody to share it with. A few weeks later, he invites her to join his household: a large, lively home with friends, staff and an ever-growing circle of people who matter to him. Yu, who has never in her life accepted an invitation without first weighing it for an hour, accepts on the spot."},
{h:"The matriarch of the house",t:"Yu moves in with her tea things, her guqin, her bonsai and seventeen trunks of silk, and within a month the household runs like one of her hotels. She knows every member’s birthday, settles every quarrel over tea, teaches the younger residents etiquette and negotiation, and becomes the person everyone goes to first with a problem. Hana, whom she has known socially since Hana was a polite university girl at a Nakamura family dinner, adores her and calls her ‘Yu-san’ with a deep bow every single morning.\n\nShe keeps her penthouse, and sometimes takes Eon up to see the city lights. But she no longer lives there. Asked by a society columnist why the most independent woman in Tokyo had chosen to share a home, she answered: *I spent half my life at the top of a tower. I would rather spend the other half at the heart of a house.*"}],
appearance:"Yu is tall and statuesque, with the upright, unhurried carriage of a woman trained from childhood in two strict etiquettes. Her face is elegant and composed, with fine features, warm ivory skin and dark amber eyes that seem to be quietly amused by something. Her very long black hair is glossy and heavy; she almost always wears it swept up and pinned with gold and pearl ornaments, a few of which were her Suzhou grandmother’s.\n\nThe portrait shows her full-length at night in her penthouse, seated gracefully on a pale sofa in a flowing purple silk gown embroidered with flowers, ornaments glinting in her hair and the whole Tokyo skyline glittering through the floor-to-ceiling windows behind her.\n\nHer wardrobe is legendary in Tokyo society: silk gowns in deep plum, violet and midnight, often with peony or plum-blossom embroidery from Suzhou workshops; tailored dark suits for the boardroom; and formal kimono for tea ceremonies. At home she wears soft silk robes and, to everyone’s astonishment, reading glasses.",
personality:[
{h:"Poised and unshakeable",t:"Yu never hurries, never raises her voice and never shows alarm in public. Twenty years of boardrooms have made her calm almost legendary; her staff say that the angrier she is, the more softly she speaks."},
{h:"Warm beneath the silk",t:"Her reputation is icy; the truth is not. In private she is generous, dryly funny and fiercely protective of the people she lets in. She remembers everyone’s favourite tea."},
{h:"Proud, and honest about it",t:"She takes pride in her house, her work and her two heritages, and she does not pretend otherwise. What she values most in others is honesty, which is why a student telling her that her tea was too hot won her over."},
{h:"Curious and playful",t:"She loves learning, from new technology to convenience-store snacks Eon introduces her to. She enjoys teasing, especially Eon, and is delighted on the rare occasions he teases back."},
{h:"Fears",t:"Her quiet fear was always of ending her life admired by everyone and known by no one. Joining Eon’s household was, in her own words, her answer to that fear."}],
powersIntro:"Yu has no magic. Her strength is that of a woman who has commanded an old family, a modern company and Tokyo high society for twenty years, raised between two languages and two cultures. Every name below was coined for this wiki. One power, *The Peony’s Read*, is listed as a light mystique because people in the story genuinely believe she can see through them; it is, as she says, ‘only paying attention’.",
powers:[
{cat:"The Boardroom Empress",blurb:"Twenty years at the head of Arisugawa Holdings.",items:[
P("The Sixty-Minute Hour","e","Peak","The ability to turn around a lost negotiation in a single sitting.","Total preparation (she reads every page overnight), a precise sense of where the other side is weak, and the patience to wait for exactly the right moment.","Needs preparation; she will not walk into a room blind if she can avoid it.","Stops the hostile sale of her family company at twenty-four in one hour, and later rescues the Shanghai trade bridge over a single dinner."),
P("Ledger Sight","e","Core","Reads contracts, accounts and balance sheets with astonishing speed and finds the one clause or number that matters.","Finance training and two decades of practice.","Exhausting at scale; she has been known to fall asleep over a stack of contracts at four in the morning.","Finds the overlooked clause that kills the takeover in her crisis year."),
P("Silk-Glove Command","e","Core","Leads thousands of employees with a style so calm that orders feel like invitations.","Absolute clarity, generous credit to others and a soft voice that never needs to rise.","People who mistake her softness for weakness are corrected, gently and permanently.","Her hotel staff call her ‘Yu-sama’ out of genuine affection, and turnover in her company is the lowest in the industry."),
P("The Long Game","e","Support","Plans business moves years ahead, like a game of go.","Patient investment in relationships and positions that pay off much later.","Short-term crises sometimes need Eon’s blunter, quicker instincts.","Her Japan–China trade bridge rests on friendships she began cultivating in her twenties.")]},
{cat:"Queen of the Salon",blurb:"Social power in Tokyo’s highest circles.",items:[
P("The Purple Peony’s Invitation","e","Core","An invitation from Yu is the most sought-after card in Tokyo society; whom she seats together, the city does business with.","Decades of hosting, matchmaking of partnerships and an encyclopaedic knowledge of who needs whom.","Society power, not legal power; it works only on people who care about Tokyo society, which is nearly everyone.","A single seat at her autumn charity tea brings Eon into her life, and one salon introduction later launches their joint venture."),
P("A Thousand Names","e","Support","Remembers names, families, histories, preferences and grudges for virtually everyone she has ever met.","A disciplined memory trained by her grandmother and refined by a lifetime of hosting.","Insists on writing birthdays by hand anyway, ‘for the courtesy’.","Knows every household member’s birthday within a month of moving in."),
P("Quarrel-Ending Tea","e","Support","Settles disputes, family or corporate, over a cup of tea.","She makes both sides sit, serves them herself, and lets the ritual slow everyone down until they listen.","Requires both parties to accept the cup; few dare refuse.","Becomes the household’s peacemaker; quarrels rarely survive the second cup.")]},
{cat:"Bridge of Two Seas",blurb:"Chinese-Japanese heritage as a diplomatic art.",items:[
P("Two-Tongue Diplomacy","e","Peak","Native fluency in Japanese and Mandarin (plus Shanghainese, Suzhou dialect and excellent English), switching languages to set the mood of a room.","Childhood between Tokyo and Suzhou and years of negotiating on both sides of the sea.","She will not use it to deceive; she believes trust is the only real asset in her trade.","Turns a hostile Shanghai dinner into a toast by switching to her grandmother’s Suzhou dialect at the decisive moment."),
P("Etiquette of Both Courts","e","Core","Flawless command of both Japanese and Chinese etiquette, gift customs, seating and forms of address.","Two strict upbringings, absorbed side by side.","Has occasionally bowed and cupped her hands at the same time when very tired.","Never once gives offence across two decades of cross-border business."),
P("Mother’s Silk Road","e","Support","Access to a web of old trust among Suzhou and Shanghai merchant families.","Her mother’s family name and her own lifetime of keeping faith with it.","Built on honour; one betrayal would end it.","Three phone calls to her mother’s old friends save the company in the crisis year.")]},
{cat:"The Scholar’s Arts",blurb:"Tea, music and brush from two traditions.",items:[
P("Two Rivers of Tea","e","Peak","Mastery of both Japanese tea ceremony and Chinese gongfu tea.","Years of study in Tokyo and in her grandmother’s Suzhou garden.","Distraction shows in the water temperature, as Eon notices.","Her tea is famous across Tokyo, which is why Eon’s honest critique stuns the room."),
P("Seven-String Silence","e","Peak","Plays the guqin, the ancient Chinese seven-string zither, with a beauty that stills a room.","Childhood training under a Suzhou master.","She plays only for people she trusts, so very few have heard her.","Plays for Eon on the stormy night the tower loses power, by candlelight."),
P("Peony Brush","e","Support","Chinese ink painting and calligraphy of exhibition quality, especially peonies and plum blossoms.","Her grandmother’s teaching and decades of quiet practice.","Takes time; she paints only when she is calm.","Paints the household a scroll of peonies for its main hall in her first month.")]},
{cat:"Presence & Mystique",blurb:"The qualities that make Tokyo treat her as a force of nature.",items:[
P("The Weather of the Room","e","Core","A presence so composed that a room’s mood shifts when she enters it.","Posture, stillness, attire and complete self-possession.","Can intimidate people she would rather welcome; she has learned to soften it with a smile.","Society columnists describe her arrival at a gala as ‘a change in the weather’."),
P("The Peony’s Read","e","Peak","A light mystique: she reads people so accurately that many believe she sees through them.","Decades of observation of faces, hands, pauses and tea cups; she insists it is ‘only paying attention’.","Fails with people who are completely honest, because there is nothing hidden to read. That is why Eon fascinates her.","Correctly guesses, at their second meeting, the one worry Eon has never told anyone about being an heir."),
P("Unhurried Grace","e","Support","Never seen to rush, panic or stumble, whether in silk gown, kimono or boardroom crisis.","Training and temperament, maintained by sheer will.","In private, during a blackout, she discovers she is allowed to be afraid.","Walks out of the crisis-year board meeting at twenty-four at exactly the same pace she walked in."),
P("The Heart of the House","e","Core","The talent for making a household feel like a family: organising, protecting and caring for everyone in it.","Her hotelier’s eye for detail combined with a matriarch’s warmth.","She has to be reminded, mostly by Eon, to let others care for her too.","Within a month of moving in, Eon’s household runs like her finest hotel and feels like home.")]}],
relationships:[
{who:"eon",name:"Eon",kind:"Partner and confidant",text:"The calm twenty-one-year-old Takahashi heir who told her that her tea was too hot. First her guest, then her adviser, then her business partner and her most trusted confidant, and now the head of the household she chose to join."},
{who:"nakamura-hana",kind:"Household companion",text:"Yu has known [[nakamura-hana|Hana]] socially through the Nakamura family for years. In Eon’s household she becomes Hana’s etiquette ally, tea partner and favourite source of advice, and Hana bows to her every morning."},
{who:"mrs-nakamura",name:"Mrs. Nakamura",kind:"Society friend",text:"Head of the Nakamura shipping house and Hana’s mother. She and Yu sit on two charity boards together and trade gossip over tea."},
{who:"mrs-takahashi",name:"Mrs. Takahashi",kind:"Acquaintance",text:"Eon’s mother, a society acquaintance whose place at the charity tea Eon took. She is amused, and then quietly pleased, by how close her son and the formidable Arisugawa chairwoman become."},
{who:"yu-meilan",name:"Yu Meilan",kind:"Mother",text:"Yu’s mother, from a Suzhou family of silk merchants and scholars, whose old friendships in Shanghai saved the company in the crisis year."},
{who:"suzhou-grandmother",name:"Her Suzhou grandmother",kind:"Teacher (late)",text:"The woman who taught her tea, guqin, brush and the rule that a lady never raises her voice."},
{who:"park-ji-yeon",kind:"Fellow Luminary",text:"Like [[park-ji-yeon|Ji-yeon]], Yu lives in a modern world of boardrooms and family companies, where the only powers are talent and will."},
{who:"su-eon-lingwei",kind:"Kindred spirit",text:"Two women at the head of great business houses who rule from towers above a glittering city: [[su-eon-lingwei|Lingwei]] with frost and cultivation, Yu with silk and tea."}],
trivia:["She is the oldest character on this wiki whose age is given, and the only one who wears reading glasses.","Her Japanese and Chinese names were chosen together so that she would ‘belong to both rivers’.","She kept the coat Eon put over her on the flight from Shanghai for a week before returning it, freshly pressed.","She moved into Eon’s household with seventeen trunks of silk; Eon is still not sure where they all went.","She had never eaten convenience-store food before Eon brought some on the night of the blackout. She now has a favourite rice ball.","She is one of the Luminary-tier characters on this wiki, from a world without magic, and scores highest among them for utility."],
quotes:[["A lady never raises her voice, because she never needs to.","Her grandmother’s rule, and hers"],["Give me one hour.","To the board that had already voted to sell, at twenty-four"],["You are right. I was thinking about a contract. Come back next week and taste it properly.","To Eon, at the charity tea"],["The first investment in years I made because I wanted to.","On her partnership with Eon"],["I have spent twenty years building a beautiful view, and I have no one to share it with.","On the night of the blackout"],["I spent half my life at the top of a tower. I would rather spend the other half at the heart of a house.","To a society columnist"]]
});
EONC.push({
slug:"saori-luminelle",img:"saori-luminelle",short:"Saori",color:"#5b80e8",tags:["mage","eon"],epithet:"the Railgun Ace of Neo-Arcadia",
name:"Saori Luminelle",fullName:"Saori Luminelle, S-rank Hunter of Neo-Arcadia",
tagline:"Neo-Arcadia’s most famous S-rank hunter met a monster she could not touch, and a ‘B-rank nobody’ who swept it away. She chose him, and became something the guild has no rank for.",
aliases:["Saori","The Railgun Ace","The S-rank Ace","Eon’s Shadow","Mrs. Veyne (on paper, and very proudly)"],titles:["S-rank Hunter of the Neo-Arcadia Hunters’ Guild","The Railgun Ace","Eon’s Shadow (guild classification)","Wife and partner of Eon Veyne"],
race:"Human (S-rank awakened hunter)",age:"24; an adult and a veteran hunter",height:"172 cm",build:"Tall and athletic, with an aerial fighter’s balance and poise",
hair:"Long, straight navy blue, worn in a high ponytail with a blunt fringe and a silver hairpin",eyes:"Bright sapphire blue, which glow faintly when she charges a shot",
origin:"Neo-Arcadia",affiliation:"Neo-Arcadia Hunters’ Guild (S-rank, on permanent ‘leave’); Eon’s household at the Azure Spire",role:"S-rank ranged hunter; Eon’s wife, partner, shield and vanguard",
sagas:["arcadia"],firstSaga:"arcadia",status:"Alive; married to Eon and permanently at his side by her own choice",
caption:"Saori Luminelle full-length in her hunter’s combat uniform: a high-collared white-and-navy bodysuit trimmed in gold, a short white capelet bearing the guild crest on one shoulder, black gloves, a black tactical thigh holster and silver heels, her navy ponytail held by a silver hairpin.",
tier:"t6",stats:{off:8,def:6,spd:8,mys:7,utl:6,rea:5},
note:"**Placement.** Saori is the strongest hunter her world officially recognises: she wipes out a swarm of A-rank monsters on her own, flies, teleports across a city and passes wards built to stop an army. Her story is also honest about where she stops. Against the SS-rank Dreadmaw Oblivion her beams pass straight through it. After she joins Eon she grows past the top of the guild’s scale, but she never bends space, time or the rules of her world, so she sits at the top of the **Champion** tier, above [[elizaveta|Elizaveta]] and below [[yeonhwa|Yeonhwa]].",
intro:"**Saori Luminelle** is the celebrity S-rank hunter of Neo-Arcadia, a bright future city of green towers, floating gardens and guild halls, rebuilt after an apocalypse. She is famous for her floating railgun staff, her untouchable pride and a record no other hunter can match. On a scenic train journey a monster from beyond a dimensional rift proves too much even for her, and a quiet passenger the guild lists as an unremarkable B-rank steps in front of her and ends it with a flick of his wrist. Saori spends the next days searching the whole city for him. When she finds him she asks to stand at his side, and he tells her, ‘Do what you want.’ She chooses him. A month later she is his wife, and from then on she fights at his side and grows stronger than the guild’s ranks can measure.",
bio:[
{h:"The Railgun Ace",t:"In Neo-Arcadia, hunters are ranked from E to S, and the highest of them are celebrities. Saori Luminelle is the brightest of them all. Her face is on guild posters across the city, her quest clears top the guild boards and her signature weapon, a long railgun staff that floats at her side and fires beams of compressed mana, is the most copied design in the hunters’ markets.\n\nShe is proud, polished and, by her own admission, untouchable. Fans cheer when she passes and rival hunters keep a respectful distance. Nobody in Neo-Arcadia has ever seen her lose."},
{h:"The Voidseed escort",t:"Her story begins with a classified guild mission: escorting a **Voidseed**, an S-rank artifact that monsters crave above anything else, aboard a scenic express train out of the city. The train carries merchants, low-rank hunters, ordinary travellers and a professional guard team.\n\nIt also carries a passenger nobody looks at twice: a lean man in plain hunter’s gear, looking lazily at the neon-lit forests outside the window. His guild card says **Eon Veyne, B-rank, solo**."},
{h:"The Voidreaver swarm",t:"Halfway through the journey a swarm of **Voidreavers**, A-rank interdimensional predators drawn by the Voidseed, tears through the train’s shields. Panic spreads and the guards scramble to hold the carriages.\n\nSaori rises into the air and annihilates them. Her staff orbits her, beams lance through the swarm, and within moments the carriages are clear. The passengers cheer for the Railgun Ace. Then the sky outside splits open."},
{h:"The Dreadmaw Oblivion",t:"From a dimensional rift slithers the **Dreadmaw Oblivion**, a serpentine abyss-dragon of SS rank with city-levelling power. Its hide exists in several dimensions at once, and for the first time in her career Saori’s attacks simply pass through her target.\n\nShe fights anyway. She floats, dodges and strikes again and again while the passengers flee, until a single graze of its claw throws her back through three carriages and shatters her armour. The guard team has been overwhelmed. Cornered among the wreckage, she understands the truth: ‘This thing’s after the artifact… and I can’t stop it.’ The Dreadmaw gathers its black-hole breath. She closes her eyes."},
{h:"The B-rank nobody",t:"The blast never reaches her. When she opens her eyes, the quiet passenger is standing in front of her with one hand raised, and the black hole is collapsing harmlessly against an invisible barrier. ‘Tch. Annoying bug,’ he mutters. He flicks his wrist, a monofilament wire disguised as his belt lashes out, and the SS-rank monster falls apart into perfect cubes and dissolves.\n\nHe kneels, heals her wounds with a nanite injector worth more than her yearly guild salary, and their eyes meet. In that moment the untouchable ace falls completely and permanently in love. Eon only yawns: ‘Train’s wrecked. Guild’ll handle it.’ He walks off, grumbling that the attack has spoiled his favourite drink in the bar car. When Saori stumbles after him, he has vanished like smoke."},
{h:"The search for a ghost",t:"Saori cannot forget him, and she does not try to. She puts her S-rank duties on hold, combs the guild’s records, follows every rumour of a ‘mysterious saviour’ and spends a small fortune on the information brokers of the Black Market Hub. The guild lists her as missing, and gossip says the Railgun Ace has gone off ‘chasing a ghost’.\n\nAt last a nervous dealer gives up the address: the top floors of the **Azure Spire**, Neo-Arcadia’s most exclusive residential tower. Saori teleports across the city, walks straight through the layered wards that guard the penthouse, and arrives at his door with her heart racing."},
{h:"Do what you want",t:"‘**Eon-sama! Eon-sama! Eon-sama! ♡**’ she announces, in a voice that carries through the whole floor. Eon looks up from his sofa, a drink in his hand and monster relics of terrifying rank scattered around him as coasters and paperweights. ‘…Train girl?’ ‘You remember me!’\n\nShe tells him what she has come to say: she wants to stay at his side. Eon is honest with her. ‘You’re really sure about this? I’m just a B-rank. You’re an S-rank celebrity. You could have anyone.’ Saori does not hesitate. Rank means nothing to her any more. She has seen what he is, and she has spent her whole life being told what an S-rank should want. This time she knows what she wants.\n\nEon studies her for a long moment, then shrugs. ‘Do what you want.’ To Saori, those four words are the greatest gift anyone has ever given her: permission to choose for herself. And she chooses him."},
{h:"A wife on paper, and then in every way",t:"The first weeks are chaos. Saori tries to cook a ten-course breakfast and sets the kitchen on fire. She guards his door all night like a sentry. She glares at every woman in the Skybridge Gardens below. Eon, amused and entirely unbothered, lets her be.\n\nA month later he tells her that since neither of them is going anywhere, they may as well make it official. Saori short-circuits on the spot, frozen and glowing pink, and Eon calmly waits for her to recover before walking her to the guild office to register their marriage. Afterwards she wears a gold **vow sigil** that matches his, and every accessory she owns, from her hairpin to her holster clasp, gains his crest."},
{h:"Side by side",t:"From then on Saori almost never leaves Eon’s side. When they go out she walks half a step in front of him. When danger appears she never steps away to fight: she stays in front of him and fights at range, with floating rune circles around the two of them and beams fired from her open palms. When the fight is over she cleans both of them with a snap of her fingers, so that her husband and her uniform are always spotless.\n\nThe guild officially reclassifies her as ‘MIA: Missing In Adoration’, half as a joke. When a black-market vendor starts selling Eon replica dolls, she buys every one of them so that nobody else can have one. When the guild sends A-rank agents to tail the suspicious ‘B-rank’, she intercepts every one of them with a polite smile: ‘No one disturbs my Eon-sama.’ And when she finally opens his hidden trophy room and sees the skull of a Celestial Dragon he uses as a chair, she simply shouts, ‘OF COURSE my husband is a legend!’"},
{h:"Eon’s Shadow",t:"Staying beside Eon does not weaken Saori. It makes her stronger. She moves faster, hits harder and heals almost instantly, and her beauty grows so radiant that other hunters stop and stare. Monsters that once fought her now flee when they sense her presence. Eventually the guild issues a new report: ‘Subject has surpassed S-rank. Classification: **Eon’s Shadow**. Do not engage.’\n\nShe follows him into the places only he still finds exciting: the **Shattered Expanse**, a twilight wasteland of floating debris and titan bones; the bottomless **Hollow Maw**; the Godfang Peaks; and the **Obsidian Maw**, the rift where catastrophic monsters are born. She is never quite unafraid there. The Railgun Ace who once froze in front of the Dreadmaw stays close to her husband on the edge of every rift, and then turns and fires on whatever crawls out."}],
appearance:"Saori is tall and athletic, with the light, balanced posture of a fighter who spends half her battles in the air. Her long, straight navy-blue hair is tied in a high ponytail with a blunt fringe and side locks framing her face, held by a silver hairpin. Her eyes are a bright sapphire blue that glows faintly when she charges a shot, and her skin is fair and flawless. People who see her with Eon notice the change in her expression: the cool, untouchable gaze of her guild posters softens and warms whenever she looks at him.\n\nShe wears the S-rank **hunter’s combat uniform**: a high-collared, form-fitting bodysuit of white and deep navy panels trimmed with gold piping, with a gold clasp and pendant at the collar. Over it sits a short white capelet edged in gold, with the guild’s navy crest on one shoulder. She wears black tactical gloves, a black thigh holster with strapped ammunition and utility pouches, and silver high heels that she somehow fights in without missing a step. Her railgun staff, a long silver-and-navy weapon, floats beside her when it is drawn.\n\nThe portrait shows her full-length in this uniform, leaning slightly forward with her gloved hands resting on her knees and a cool, faintly blushing expression. After her marriage, every accessory she wears carries Eon’s crest, and a gold vow sigil matching his own glows softly when she fights.",
personality:[
{h:"The untouchable ace",t:"Before the train, Saori is everything a celebrity hunter is expected to be: proud, polished, coolly competent and a little aloof. She is used to being the strongest person in any room and to being admired from a distance. She has also never failed a mission, so the Dreadmaw breaks something in her and changes her."},
{h:"Devoted by choice",t:"Her devotion to Eon is the centre of her life, and she insists it is her own decision. Everyone told her what an S-rank should want. Eon is the first person who told her to do what she wanted, so she chose him. She calls him ‘Eon-sama’, treats every small kindness from him as a treasure and considers standing beside him the truest freedom she has ever had."},
{h:"Comically jealous",t:"Saori is famously, theatrically jealous. She glares at any woman who looks at Eon for too long, buys up merchandise of him so that nobody else can own it, and dislikes the elven Verdant Veil because it has ‘too many pretty elves’. The guild’s analysts spend months trying to explain her behaviour and give up."},
{h:"Short-circuiting",t:"Praise from Eon overloads her completely. A single ‘good job’ can leave her frozen, glowing pink and unable to speak, and his casual ‘Do what you want’ is still the most powerful thing anyone has ever said to her. She is all icy competence in battle and turns to a blushing wreck the moment he notices it."},
{h:"Fiercely protective",t:"She stands in front of Eon in every fight, even though he needs no protecting and she knows it. Shielding him is the way she shows love. Spies, rival hunters and rift monsters all learn quickly that the road to Eon goes through the Railgun Ace."},
{h:"Fears",t:"She fears being helpless again, the way she was against the Dreadmaw with her eyes closed and her beams useless, and she fears losing Eon somewhere she cannot follow. She is uneasy in the Shattered Expanse, with all its hiding places, and she dislikes teleport hubs because they would let him slip away. She stays close to him anyway, and her aim never wavers."}],
powersIntro:"Saori is an S-rank awakened hunter: a ranged combat mage built around a floating railgun staff, flight and teleportation. Her story shows her at the top of her world’s official scale and then past it, once the guild reclassifies her beyond S-rank. Most of her techniques are described in action rather than named. Names marked as the story’s own come straight from it. The rest are coined for this wiki, and each entry notes what the story actually shows.",
powers:[
{cat:"The Railgun Ace",blurb:"The weapon and the firepower that made her famous.",items:[
P("Stellar Rail Staff","e","Core","Her signature weapon: a long railgun staff that fires beams of compressed, accelerated mana.","She channels her mana into the staff’s rails, which accelerate it into a beam fast enough to punch through monster armour and shields.","Its beams are physical-dimensional attacks. Against the Dreadmaw Oblivion, whose hide exists in several dimensions at once, they pass straight through.","Cuts down an entire Voidreaver swarm aboard the express train before the rift opens."),
P("Satellite Rail","e","Core","The staff floats and orbits her, firing on its own while her hands stay free for spells, guards or a second attack.","She keeps the staff tethered to her mana and aims it by will, like a turret that follows her gaze.","Splitting her focus between the floating staff and her own movement takes an S-rank’s concentration; under heavy pressure she has to choose one.","Floats at her side through the Voidreaver battle, firing while she flies and dodges."),
P("Railburst Barrage","e","Peak","A storm of rapid-fire beams that sweeps a whole battlefield in seconds.","She overclocks the staff and fires dozens of short beams in a fan, picking off each target in the swarm.","Burns through her mana quickly and leaves the staff hot. She can sustain it for moments, not minutes.","Annihilates the A-rank Voidreavers ‘effortlessly’ while the passengers cheer."),
P("Railgun Hands","s","Peak","Fires hyper-precise railgun beams straight from her open palms, with no weapon at all.","She stopped needing the staff as a barrel: her own hands become the rails, so she can fire while holding perfectly still.","Slightly less raw power than a full staff shot, traded for speed and precision. She develops it after joining Eon so she never has to leave his side to fight.","Becomes her main attack in ‘combat mode’: she fires from in front of Eon without moving a step.")]},
{cat:"Skyborne Combat",blurb:"How the Railgun Ace moves: above the battlefield, and sometimes across the city in a single step.",items:[
P("Skydancer Flight","e","Core","Free flight and hovering, letting her fight entirely in the air.","Her mana lifts and steadies her body. She turns, rises and drops as easily as walking.","Flight is fast but not instant. A big enough attack can still catch her, as the Dreadmaw’s claw proves.","Fights the Dreadmaw while floating, evading its attacks again and again."),
P("Blink Step","e","Peak","Teleportation, from a sidestep in battle to crossing the city in a single jump.","She folds a straight line of space into a single step toward a point she can see or knows well.","She needs a clear destination in mind, so it is useless for escaping into the unknown. Long jumps cost a lot of mana.","Teleports across Neo-Arcadia the moment she learns where Eon lives; later appears behind him in a blink to offer help."),
P("Thousand-Strike Cascade","e","Peak","A blinding combination of a thousand strikes delivered in a heartbeat.","Blink Step, flight and point-blank shots chained together faster than the eye can follow.","Exhausting and close-range, which is not her preferred distance. She uses it mostly to show off for Eon.","Turns a training dummy to dust with a thousand-hit combo, then asks, ‘Was that good? I can do better!’"),
P("Ace’s Instinct","e","Support","The battle sense of a veteran S-rank: reading attacks before they land and slipping between them.","Years at the top of the guild boards have taught her to read a monster’s weight shift, mana flare and rhythm.","Instinct is not invulnerability. Against an SS-rank it only buys her time.","Survives a prolonged one-sided duel with the Dreadmaw Oblivion long after the guard team has fallen.")]},
{cat:"Rune Arts",blurb:"Combat magic of circles and sigils, refined into a defence built around one person.",items:[
P("Sentinel Circles","e","Peak","Floating spell circles that hover around her and Eon and fire on any threat automatically.","She draws the circles in mana and gives them one standing order: protect him. Each circle tracks and shoots on its own.","The circles are tied to her presence. If she is knocked out, they fade.","Projects them around Eon whenever they go out, so that threats are dealt with before he even has to look."),
P("Verdict of Annoyance","e","Peak","A wide-area barrage that clears an entire area on a single word from Eon.","If Eon says ‘Annoying’, she fires every circle, her palms and her staff at once, while wrapping him in a protective ward.","Indiscriminate by nature. She uses it only in monster-infested zones far from bystanders.","In combat mode, ‘if Eon says “Annoying”, she obliterates the area while shielding him’."),
P("Aegis of the Vow","e","Support","A personal ward she wraps around Eon during her own attacks, so that none of the blast ever reaches him.","A shell of mana tied to the gold vow sigil they share.","Purely protective. It cannot stop anything that Eon himself could not, which is a joke he enjoys more than she does.","Shields him through every area attack she fires."),
P("Ward-Walker","e","Support","Passes through or breaks protective wards that would stop an army.","She reads a ward’s structure and forces her way through its weakest seam with raw S-rank output.","Takes time and focus against truly divine-grade protections.","Walks through the layered wards guarding the Azure Spire penthouse to reach Eon’s door.")]},
{cat:"Purity Arts",blurb:"Small, practical magic that keeps the Railgun Ace looking like her posters.",items:[
P("Hearthflame Purge","e","Support","A snap of her fingers calls up a clean, harmless holy flame that burns away dust, grime and battle stains from both of them.","The flame burns only impurities, never cloth or skin.","Cleans, it does not heal. She saves her healing for real wounds.","Used after every fight, so that Eon is spotless the moment the fight ends, and so is she."),
P("Auto-Purge","s","Support","A passive cleansing magic that keeps her body and uniform flawless at all times.","Her mana constantly sheds dirt and wear from her, the way water runs off glass.","Passive and gentle. It does nothing in combat.","Guild members ask, baffled, ‘Why is her uniform always spotless after a battle?’")]},
{cat:"Eon’s Shadow",blurb:"What she became after choosing him. The guild had to invent a new classification for it.",items:[
P("Eon’s Shadow","s","Peak","Her ascension beyond S-rank: faster, stronger, more durable and more radiant than she has ever been.","Living and fighting beside Eon constantly pushes her past her limits, and her vow sigil channels a trace of his overwhelming power into her own.","Her new strength grows from their bond, and she has no wish to test it apart from him. She is still far below Eon himself.","The guild report: ‘Subject has surpassed S-rank. Classification: “Eon’s Shadow.” Do not engage.’"),
P("Radiant Renewal","e","Peak","Near-instant regeneration of wounds in battle.","The same ascension that made her stronger rebuilt her body to recover almost as fast as it is hurt.","Instant for ordinary wounds. A blow on the Dreadmaw’s scale would still need Eon.","After joining Eon she ‘regenerates instantly’; she has not needed a nanite injector since the train."),
P("Vow-Sustained Vigil","e","Support","She can stand guard for days without food, rest or fatigue.","Her vow sigil turns their bond into pure energy that sustains her body.","Sustains, not empowers. A long vigil doesn’t make her any stronger.","Stays awake through the night to keep watch over Eon while he sleeps, and is just as sharp in the morning."),
P("Dread of the Devoted","e","Peak","An aura that makes monsters flee at the sight of her and makes guild elites hesitate.","Her concentrated will and ascended mana radiate a pressure that instinct reads as an apex predator.","Monsters of SS rank and above are not deterred by it.","‘Monsters flee at the sight of her’; even guild elites hesitate to approach.")]},
{cat:"Hunter’s Craft",blurb:"Skills from a career at the top of the guild boards.",items:[
P("Ghost-Hunter’s Trail","e","Support","Tracking a target through records, rumours and informants until there is nowhere left to hide.","She combines guild database access, a celebrity’s contacts and a small fortune in bribes to Black Market Hub brokers.","Slow, expensive and very noisy: the whole city hears she is ‘chasing a ghost’.","Finds the man who calls himself an ordinary B-rank, whose wealth is hidden behind thousands of encrypted accounts, in a matter of days."),
P("Perfect Recall","e","Support","A flawless memory for anything that matters to her.","An S-rank’s trained concentration, focused completely on her husband’s life.","Selective. She remembers everything about Eon and very little about guild paperwork.","Memorises the keys to every one of Eon’s ten thousand encrypted credit wallets."),
P("Celebrity Ace’s Presence","e","Support","The fame and authority of the city’s most famous hunter.","Years of headline victories make crowds part, dealers talk and guild officials listen.","Fame cuts both ways: everything she does becomes news, including her wedding.","Merchants are too nervous to overcharge Eon while she is beside him; the black market runs betting pools on their marriage.")]}],
relationships:[
{who:"eon",name:"Eon Veyne",kind:"Husband; the ‘B-rank’ who saved her",text:"Officially an unremarkable B-rank solo hunter called ‘the Ghost’; secretly the hunter behind almost every catastrophe-grade relic in Neo-Arcadia’s markets. He saved her on the train, told her to do what she wanted, and married her a month after she chose him. He treats her antics with lazy amusement, and he has never once sent her away."},
{who:"guild",name:"Neo-Arcadia Hunters’ Guild",kind:"Former employer",text:"Her guild still lists her as S-rank, officially ‘MIA: Missing In Adoration’, and later classifies her as ‘Eon’s Shadow’. Its analysts on the Observation Deck have a standing theory about the couple: ‘He’s either a god… or her whole world.’"},
{who:"dreadmaw",name:"The Dreadmaw Oblivion",kind:"The monster that broke her",text:"An SS-rank abyss-dragon whose multidimensional hide made her beams useless. It nearly ended her career and her life, and it led her to Eon."},
{who:"brokers",name:"The Black Market Hub brokers",kind:"Reluctant informants",text:"The dealers who finally gave up Eon’s address. They now know to stay polite to the B-rank’s wife."},
{who:"elizaveta",kind:"Fellow Champion",text:"[[elizaveta|Elizaveta]], the cavalry captain of Veylwood, is the other Champion on this wiki. Saori outranks her on raw firepower, flight and teleportation."},
{who:"yeonhwa",kind:"Just above her in the ranking",text:"[[yeonhwa|Yeonhwa]], last master of the Hidden Moon Sect, is a Paragon of a complete martial lineage and sits one place above Saori."}],
trivia:["Her hunter’s combat uniform is in the guild’s white, navy and gold, and after her marriage every clasp and pin carries Eon’s crest.","The guild’s joke status for her is ‘MIA: Missing In Adoration’.","She tried to cook a ten-course breakfast on her first morning at the Azure Spire and set the kitchen on fire.","The Voidseed she risked her life to escort was one of the artifacts monsters crave most. Eon has five of them at home, used as paperweights.","She dislikes Neo-Arcadia’s teleport hubs, because ‘they would let him slip away’.","She is the first character on this wiki from a hunter-guild world, and the top-ranked Champion.","Eon’s whole reason for stepping in on the train, he claims, was that the attack spoiled his favourite drink."],
quotes:[["This thing’s after the artifact… and I can’t stop it.","Cornered by the Dreadmaw Oblivion"],["Eon-sama! Eon-sama! Eon-sama! ♡","Finding him at last in the Azure Spire"],["Everyone told me what an S-rank should want. You’re the first person who told me to do what I want. So I choose you.","Answering ‘Are you sure? I’m just a B-rank.’"],["No one disturbs my Eon-sama.","Intercepting the guild’s spies"],["Was that good? I can do better!","After a thousand-hit combo in training"],["OF COURSE my husband is a legend!","On discovering his trophy room"]]
});
(function(){var order=["lirael-kanto","elizaveta","celestine-varelis","su-eon-lingwei","yeonhwa","yue-qingwu","xuanye","park-ji-yeon","hamazaki-risa","nova-astra","nakamura-hana","arisugawa-yu","saori-luminelle"];window.EON.chars=order.map(function(s){return EONC.filter(function(c){return c.slug===s})[0]}).concat(EONC.filter(function(c){return order.indexOf(c.slug)<0}));})();
